 shortest palindrome starting with a given string.\n- **CLI Tool**: Command-line interface for easy interaction.\n- **Persistence**: Optionally save a history of generated palindromes.\n- **Configurable**: Ignore case and/or whitespace for checks and generation.\n- **Developer-friendly**: Modular design, unit-tested, and importable as a library.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install the package using `pip` (or `poetry`):\n\n```bash\npip install .\n# Or if using poetry for development:\n# poetry install\n```\n\n## Usage (CLI)\n\nThe CLI tool is available via the `palindrome` command.\n\n### Check if a string is a palindrome\n\n```bash\npalindrome check \"racecar\"\n# Expected output:\n# true\n\npalindrome check \"hello\"\n# Expected output:\n# false\n\npalindrome check \"A man a plan a canal Panama\" --normalize-case --normalize-whitespace\n# Expected output:\n# true\n```\n\n### Generate the shortest palindrome\n\nThis command will also record the operation in history if `--persist` is enabled.\n\n```bash\npalindrome make \"cat\"\n# Expected output:\n# catac\n\npalindrome make \"A\" --persist\n# Expected output:\n# A\n\npalindrome make \"hello world\" --normalize-case --normalize-whitespace --persist\n# Expected output:\n# helloworldlrowolleh\n```\n\n### List history\n\n```bash\npalindrome history\n# Expected output (example):\n# [2023-10-27T10:30:00.000Z] Input: 'A' -> Result: 'A' (ID: ...)\n# [2023-10-27T10:31:00.000Z] Input: 'hello world' -> Result: 'helloworldlrowolleh' (ID: ...)\n\npalindrome history --limit 1 --json\n# Expected output (example):\n# [\n#   {\n#     \"id\": \"...\",\n#     \"input_text\": \"hello world\",\n#     \"result_text\": \"helloworldlrowolleh\",\n#     \"timestamp\": \"2023-10-27T10:31:00.000Z\"\n#   }\n# ]\n```\n\n### Global Options\n\nThese options can be used with `check` and `make` commands:\n\n- `--normalize-case`: Ignore case when checking or generating palindromes.\n- `--normalize-whitespace`: Collapse multiple spaces into a single space and strip leading/trailing whitespace.\n- `--persist`: Enable persistence for the `make` command.\n- `--history-path FILE`: Specify a custom path for the history JSON file.\n\n## Usage (Library)\n\nYou can import and use the functionality in your Python code:\n\n```python\nfrom palindrome_app import PalindromeService, Config, Utils\n\n# Using raw utility functions (no normalization or persistence)\nprint(Utils.is_palindrome(\"madam\")) # True\nprint(Utils.make_palindrome(\"banana\")) # bananab\n\n# Using the service layer (with configuration options)\nconfig = Config(normalize_case=True, normalize_whitespace=True, persist=True)\nservice = PalindromeService(config)\n\n# Check a palindrome with normalization\nprint(service.is_palindrome(\"Race Car\")) # True\n\n# Generate a palindrome with normalization and persist\nresult = service.compute_and_record(\"hello world\")\nprint(result.result_text) # helloworldlrowolleh\n\n# List history\nhistory_records = service.list_history(limit=5)\nfor record in history_records:\n    print(f\"{record.input_text} -> {record.result_text}\")\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .github/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 workflows/\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 ci.yml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 palindrome_app/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 repositories.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 main.py\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 tests/\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_utils.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_services.py\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_repositories.py\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_cli_integration.py\n```\n\n### Running Tests\n\nTo run the unit and integration tests:\n\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n### CI/CD\n\nA GitHub Actions workflow is provided in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` to run tests automatically on pushes and pull requests.\n\n## Contributing\n\nPlease refer to the project's issue tracker for any bugs or feature requests.\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License.\n```\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n        uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n        with:\n          python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n          cache: 'poetry'\n\n      - name: Install Poetry\n        run: pip install poetry\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: poetry install --no-root --with dev\n\n      - name: Run tests\n        run: poetry run pytest\n\n      # Optional: Add linting step\n      # - name: Lint with Flake8\n      #   run: |\n      #     pip install flake8\n      #     flake8 src/\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\npalindrome_app: A reusable Python library and CLI tool for palindrome operations.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .models import PalindromeResult, HistoryRecord\nfrom .exceptions import PalindromeError, ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .utils import Utils\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom .services import PalindromeService\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/config.py\n\"\"\"\nModule for application configuration management.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Optional\nimport os\n\n# Function to approximate cross-platform user data directory paths\ndef _get_default_user_data_dir(app_name: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Returns a platform-specific default directory for application data.\"\"\"\n    if os.name == 'posix': # Linux, macOS, other Unix-like\n        # Prefer XDG_DATA_HOME or ~/.local/share\n        xdg_data_home = os.environ.get('XDG_DATA_HOME')\n        if xdg_data_home:\n            return os.path.join(xdg_data_home, app_name)\n        else:\n            return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser('~'), '.local', 'share', app_name)\n    elif os.name == 'nt': # Windows\n        app_data = os.environ.get('APPDATA')\n        if app_data:\n            return os.path.join(app_data, app_name)\n        else: # Fallback for less common Windows setups\n            return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser('~'), 'AppData', 'Roaming', app_name)\n    else: # Generic fallback\n        return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser('~'), '.' + app_name)\n\n\nDEFAULT_HISTORY_FILENAME = \"history.json\"\nAPP_NAME = \"palindrome_app\"\n\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Centralized configuration for the palindrome application.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self,\n                 persist: bool = False,\n                 history_path: Optional[str] = None,\n                 normalize_case: bool = False,\n                 normalize_whitespace: bool = False) -> None:\n        self.persist = persist\n        self.history_path = history_path\n        self.normalize_case = normalize_case\n        self.normalize_whitespace = normalize_whitespace\n\n    def resolve_history_path(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Resolves the full path to the history file based on configuration.\"\"\"\n        if self.history_path:\n            # If an explicit path is given, use it (and make it absolute)\n            return os.path.abspath(self.history_path)\n        else:\n            # Use the default user data directory\n            default_dir = _get_default_user_data_dir(APP_NAME)\n            return os.path.join(default_dir, DEFAULT_HISTORY_FILENAME)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/models.py\n\"\"\"\nModule for domain data transfer objects (DTOs).\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nclass PalindromeResult:\n    \"\"\"Represents the result of a palindrome operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, input_text: str, result_text: str, is_palindrome: bool, timestamp: str) -> None:\n        self.input_text = input_text\n        self.result_text = result_text\n        self.is_palindrome = is_palindrome\n        self.timestamp = timestamp\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Converts the result to a dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"input_text\": self.input_text,\n            \"result_text\": self.result_text,\n            \"is_palindrome\": self.is_palindrome,\n            \"timestamp\": self.timestamp,\n        }\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_dict(d: Dict[str, Any]) -> \"PalindromeResult\":\n        \"\"\"Creates a PalindromeResult instance from a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return PalindromeResult(\n            input_text=str(d[\"input_text\"]),\n            result_text=str(d[\"result_text\"]),\n            is_palindrome=bool(d[\"is_palindrome\"]),\n            timestamp=str(d[\"timestamp\"]),\n        )\n\nclass HistoryRecord:\n    \"\"\"Represents a persisted history record of an operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, id: str, input_text: str, result_text: str, timestamp: str) -> None:\n        self.id = id\n        self.input_text = input_text\n        self.result_text = result_text\n        self.timestamp = timestamp\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, str]:\n        \"\"\"Converts the record to a dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"id\": self.id,\n            \"input_text\": self.input_text,\n            \"result_text\": self.result_text,\n            \"timestamp\": self.timestamp,\n        }\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_dict(d: Dict[str, str]) -> \"HistoryRecord\":\n        \"\"\"Creates a HistoryRecord instance from a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return HistoryRecord(\n            id=str(d[\"id\"]),\n            input_text=str(d[\"input_text\"]),\n            result_text=str(d[\"result_text\"]),\n            timestamp=str(d[\"timestamp\"]),\n        )\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nModule for domain-specific exception classes.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass PalindromeError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for palindrome application errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"An unexpected palindrome error occurred.\") -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\nclass ValidationError(PalindromeError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input data.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input validation failed.\") -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass PersistenceError(PalindromeError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for errors during data persistence operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Failed to persist data.\") -> None:\n        super().__init>(message)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/utils.py\n\"\"\"\nModule containing core palindrome algorithms as pure functions.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass Utils:\n    \"\"\"Provides static utility methods for palindrome operations.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_palindrome(s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Test if given string is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        return s == s[::-1]\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _longest_palindromic_suffix(s: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the starting index of the longest palindromic suffix.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(s)):\n            suffix = s[i:]\n            if suffix == suffix[::-1]:\n                return i\n        return len(s) - 1 # If no multi-char suffix is found, the last char is a palindrome.\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def make_palindrome(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\"\"\"\n        if s == \"\":\n            return \"\"\n        # Find the index where the longest palindromic suffix begins.\n        i = Utils._longest_palindromic_suffix(s)\n        prefix_to_reverse = s[:i]\n        return s + prefix_to_reverse[::-1]\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/repositories.py\n\"\"\"\nModule for file-based JSON history persistence.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom tempfile import NamedTemporaryFile\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .models import HistoryRecord\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\n\nDEFAULT_ENCODING = \"utf-8\"\n\nclass HistoryRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages reading and writing history records to a JSON file.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, path: str) -> None:\n        self.path = path\n\n    def save(self, record: HistoryRecord) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a history record to the JSON file, creating it if necessary.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            # Ensure the directory for the history file exists\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self.path), exist_ok=True)\n\n            records_data = []\n            if os.path.exists(self.path):\n                with open(self.path, \"r\", encoding=DEFAULT_ENCODING) as f:\n                    try:\n                        records_data = json.load(f)\n                        if not isinstance(records_data, list):\n                            # If file exists but is not a list, treat as corrupted\n                            records_data = []\n                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                        # File is corrupted JSON, start with empty list\n                        records_data = []\n\n            records_data.append(record.to_dict())\n\n            # Perform an atomic write to prevent data corruption during write\n            with NamedTemporaryFile(mode=\"w\", delete=False, encoding=DEFAULT_ENCODING) as tmp_file:\n                json.dump(records_data, tmp_file, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n            os.replace(tmp_file.name, self.path) # Atomically replace the old file with the new one\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to save history record to '{self.path}': {e}\")\n\n    def list(self, limit: Optional[int] = None) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Reads and returns history records, latest first, with optional limit.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            if not os.path.exists(self.path):\n                return []\n\n            with open(self.path, \"r\", encoding=DEFAULT_ENCODING) as f:\n                records_data = json.load(f)\n\n            if not isinstance(records_data, list):\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"History file '{self.path}' contains invalid data format (not a list).\")\n\n            # Convert dicts to HistoryRecord objects and reverse to show latest first\n            history_records = [HistoryRecord.from_dict(d) for d in records_data]\n            history_records.reverse()\n\n            if limit:\n                return history_records[:limit]\n            return history_records\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"History file '{self.path}' is corrupted or invalid JSON: {e}\")\n        except FileNotFoundError: # This might occur between os.path.exists and open\n            return []\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to list history records from '{self.path}': {e}\")\n\n    def find_by_input(self, input_text: str) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Finds and returns history records whose input_text matches the given text.\"\"\"\n        all_records = self.list(limit=None) # Get all records\n        return [record for record in all_records if record.input_text == input_text]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/services.py\n\"\"\"\nModule for application-level operations and business logic.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport uuid\n\nfrom .models import PalindromeResult, HistoryRecord\nfrom .utils import Utils\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\n\nclass PalindromeService:\n    \"\"\"Provides core business logic for palindrome operations, including persistence.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, config: Config, repository: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None) -> None:\n        self.config = config\n        self.repository = repository\n        # If persistence is enabled but no repository is provided, create one with the resolved path.\n        if self.config.persist and self.repository is None:\n            try:\n                self.repository = HistoryRepository(self.config.resolve_history_path())\n            except Exception as e:\n                # If repository creation fails, log and disable persistence for this service instance\n                print(f\"Warning: Failed to initialize HistoryRepository: {e}. Persistence disabled.\", file=sys.stderr)\n                self.repository = None\n                self.config.persist = False\n\n\n    def _normalize_input(self, s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Applies configured normalization rules to the input string.\"\"\"\n        if self.config.normalize_case:\n            s = s.lower()\n        if self.config.normalize_whitespace:\n            # Replaces multiple whitespaces with single space and strips leading/trailing\n            s = \" \".join(s.split())\n        return s\n\n    def is_palindrome(self, s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a string is a palindrome after applying normalization.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input for palindrome check must be a string.\")\n        normalized_s = self._normalize_input(s)\n        return Utils.is_palindrome(normalized_s)\n\n    def make_palindrome(self, s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Produces the shortest palindrome beginning with the supplied string after normalization.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input for palindrome generation must be a string.\")\n        normalized_s = self._normalize_input(s)\n        return Utils.make_palindrome(normalized_s)\n\n    def compute_and_record(self, s: str) -> PalindromeResult:\n        \"\"\"Computes palindrome status/generation and optionally records the operation.\"\"\"\n        # Check if the normalized version of the input is a palindrome\n        is_pal_check_for_result = self.is_palindrome(s) # This calls _normalize_input internally\n\n        # Determine the result_text based on the normalized string operations\n        normalized_input_for_ops = self._normalize_input(s)\n        if Utils.is_palindrome(normalized_input_for_ops):\n            result_text = normalized_input_for_ops\n        else:\n            result_text = Utils.make_palindrome(normalized_input_for_ops)\n\n        # Use current UTC time in ISO-8601 format with milliseconds and 'Z' for Zulu time\n        timestamp = datetime.utcnow().isoformat(timespec='milliseconds') + \"Z\"\n\n        pr = PalindromeResult(input_text=s, result_text=result_text, is_palindrome=is_pal_check_for_result, timestamp=timestamp)\n\n        # Persist the record if the repository is available and persistence is configured\n        if self.config.persist and self.repository:\n            record = HistoryRecord(id=str(uuid.uuid4()), input_text=s, result_text=result_text, timestamp=timestamp)\n            try:\n                self.repository.save(record)\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                # Propagate PersistenceError, CLI will handle\n                raise\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Catch unexpected errors during save and wrap them\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"An unexpected error occurred during history save: {e}\")\n\n        return pr\n\n    def list_history(self, limit: Optional[int] = None) -> List[HistoryRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Lists historical palindrome operations, with optional limit.\"\"\"\n        if not self.repository:\n            # If no repository or persistence is off, return an empty list\n            return []\n        try:\n            return self.repository.list(limit=limit)\n        except PersistenceError:\n            # Propagate PersistenceError, CLI will handle\n            raise\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch unexpected errors during list and wrap them\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"An unexpected error occurred while listing history: {e}\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/controllers.py\n\"\"\"\nModule for CLI controller and argument parsing.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .services import PalindromeService\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .models import HistoryRecord, PalindromeResult\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface interactions, dispatching commands to the service.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, service: PalindromeService) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n\n    def run(self, args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the requested command based on parsed arguments and prints results.\n        'args' is an argparse.Namespace object containing all parsed CLI arguments.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            if args.command == \"check\":\n                # For 'check', we only need the boolean result. No persistence logic for 'check' command directly.\n                is_pal = self.service.is_palindrome(args.text)\n                print(str(is_pal).lower())\n                return 0\n\n            elif args.command == \"make\":\n                # For 'make', we compute and record. Persistence is handled by the service if configured via global flags.\n                result: PalindromeResult = self.service.compute_and_record(args.text)\n                print(result.result_text)\n                return 0\n\n            elif args.command == \"history\":\n                # For 'history', list records. Global normalization flags do not apply here.\n                records: List[HistoryRecord] = self.service.list_history(limit=args.limit)\n                if args.json:\n                    # Output as a JSON array of records\n                    print(json.dumps([r.to_dict() for r in records], ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\n                else:\n                    for r in records:\n                        print(f\"[{r.timestamp}] Input: '{r.input_text}' -> Result: '{r.result_text}' (ID: {r.id})\")\n                return 0\n\n            else:\n                # This case should ideally not be reached due to 'required=True' on subparsers in main's parser.\n                # However, as a safety, print help and exit.\n                print(\"Error: Unknown command.\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Invalid input: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            # According to FR4: CLI surfaces message but continues unless configured to fail.\n            # Here, we print error and return non-zero exit code as a failure.\n            print(f\"Error: Persistence failed: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error: An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n```\n\n```python\n# src/palindrome_app/main.py\n\"\"\"\nMain entry point for the palindrome CLI application.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport argparse\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .config import Config, APP_NAME, DEFAULT_HISTORY_FILENAME\nfrom .services import PalindromeService\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\nfrom .exceptions import PalindromeError, PersistenceError\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs application components and runs the CLI controller.\n    Parses all command-line arguments to configure the application.\n    \"\"\"\n    argv = argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:]\n\n    # Define the full argparse parser here, including global and subcommand arguments.\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        prog=\"palindrome\",\n        description=\"CLI tool to check and generate palindromes, with optional history persistence.\"\n    )\n\n    # Global optional arguments for configuration\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--normalize-case\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Ignore case when checking or generating palindromes.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--normalize-whitespace\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Collapse multiple spaces into a single space and strip leading/trailing whitespace.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--persist\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Enable persistence for the 'make' command.\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--history-path\",\n        type=str,\n        help=f\"Custom path for the history JSON file. Defaults to {APP_NAME}/{DEFAULT_HISTORY_FILENAME} in user data directory.\"\n    )\n\n    subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True, help=\"Available commands\")\n\n    # 'check' subcommand parser\n    check_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n        \"check\",\n        help=\"Check if a string is a palindrome.\"\n    )\n    check_parser.add_argument(\n        \"text\",\n        type=str,\n        help=\"The string to check.\"\n    )\n\n    # 'make' subcommand parser\n    make_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n        \"make\",\n        help=\"Generate the shortest palindrome that starts with the given string.\"\n    )\n    make_parser.add_argument(\n        \"text\",\n        type=str,\n        help=\"The string to use as the base for palindrome generation.\"\n    )\n\n    # 'history' subcommand parser\n    history_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n        \"history\",\n        help=\"List previously recorded palindrome operations.\"\n    )\n    history_parser.add_argument(\n        \"--limit\",\n        type=int,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"Limit the number of history records to display (most recent first).\"\n    )\n    history_parser.add_argument(\n        \"--json\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Output history in JSON format.\"\n    )\n\n    try:\n        # Parse all command-line arguments\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        # Construct Config object based on parsed global arguments\n        app_config = Config(\n            persist=args.persist,\n            history_path=args.history_path,\n            normalize_case=args.normalize_case,\n            normalize_whitespace=args.normalize_whitespace\n        )\n\n        # Construct HistoryRepository if persistence is enabled in config\n        history_repository: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None\n        if app_config.persist:\n            try:\n                # Attempt to create repository, handle potential path resolution errors\n                history_repository = HistoryRepository(app_config.resolve_history_path())\n            except Exception as e:\n                # If repository setup fails, print a warning and proceed without persistence.\n                # The service will then be initialized with a None repository.\n                print(f\"Warning: Could not set up history persistence due to: {e}. Running without history.\", file=sys.stderr)\n                app_config.persist = False # Ensure service knows persistence is off\n                history_repository = None\n\n\n        # Construct PalindromeService with the configured Config and optional HistoryRepository\n        palindrome_service = PalindromeService(config=app_config, repository=history_repository)\n\n        # Construct CLIController\n        cli_controller = CLIController(service=palindrome_service)\n\n        # Run the controller with the parsed arguments object\n        return cli_controller.run(args)\n\n    except PalindromeError as e:\n        # Catch any specific PalindromeError not handled by CLIController for general CLI errors\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n    except SystemExit as e:\n        # argparse sometimes raises SystemExit directly for help messages or errors\n        return e.code\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Catch any other unexpected critical errors\n        print(f\"Error: An unexpected critical error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return 1\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n```"}
