{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string representing musical notes in a special ASCII format.\n    Your task is to parse this string and return list of integers corresponding to how many beats does each\n    not last.\n\n    Here is a legend:\n    'o' - whole note, lasts four beats\n    'o|' - half note, lasts two beats\n    '.|' - quater note, lasts one beat\n\n    >>> parse_music('o o| .| o| o| .| .| .| .| o o')\n    [4, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Define the mapping from note tokens to their beat durations.\n    beat_map = {\n        'o': 4,\n        'o|': 2,\n        '.|': 1\n    }\n\n    # Split the music string into individual tokens, handling any leading/trailing whitespace.\n    tokens = music_string.strip().split()\n\n    # Map each token to its corresponding beat value.\n    # Per requirements, trust inputs and do not add explicit error checks for unknown tokens.\n    beats = [beat_map[token] for token in tokens]\n\n    return beats\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\n# src/musicparser/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Music parser package, exposing the primary parse_music function.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .services import ParserService\nfrom .exceptions import ParseError\nfrom .config import VERSION\n\n# Initialize a default service instance for the convenience function\n_default_service = ParserService()\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a musical notation string into a list of integer beat durations.\n    Delegates to the ParserService for core logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _default_service.parse_music(music_string)\n\n__all__ = [\"parse_music\", \"ParseError\", \"VERSION\"]\n\n# src/musicparser/config.py\n\"\"\"Configuration constants for the music parser.\"\"\"\n\nNOTE_TO_BEATS: dict[str, int] = {\"o\": 4, \"o|\": 2, \".|\": 1}\nSUPPORTED_TOKENS: set[str] = set(NOTE_TO_BEATS.keys())\nVERSION = \"0.1.0\"\n\n# src/musicparser/exceptions.py\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass ParseError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for errors during music notation parsing.\n    Stores contextual information like the problematic token and its position.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, token: Optional[str] = None, position: Optional[int] = None) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.token = token\n        self.position = position\n\n# src/musicparser/models.py\n\"\"\"Domain models for musical notes.\"\"\"\n\nclass Note:\n    \"\"\"Represents a recognized musical note type with its name and beat duration.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, name: str, beats: int) -> None:\n        self._name = name\n        self._beats = beats\n\n    @property\n    def name(self) -> str:\n        return self._name\n\n    @property\n    def beats(self) -> int:\n        return self._beats\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict[str, int | str]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a dictionary representation of the note.\"\"\"\n        return {\"name\": self._name, \"beats\": self._beats}\n\n# src/musicparser/utils.py\n\"\"\"Utility functions for the music parser.\"\"\"\n\ndef normalize_token(token: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Normalizes a token string by stripping whitespace.\n    This function centralizes future normalization logic if needed.\n    \"\"\"\n    return token.strip()\n\n# src/musicparser/tokenizer.py\nimport re\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\nfrom .exceptions import ParseError\nfrom .utils import normalize_token\n\nclass Tokenizer:\n    \"\"\"Splits a musical notation string into a list of normalized tokens with their original positions.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        pass # No complex regex needed for simple whitespace splitting\n\n    def tokenize(self, music: str) -> List[Tuple[str, int]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Tokenizes the input string into (token, position) pairs.\n        Returns an empty list for empty or whitespace-only input.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(music, str):\n            raise ParseError(\"Input must be a string\", token=None, position=None)\n\n        trimmed_music = music.strip()\n        if not trimmed_music:\n            return []\n\n        # str.split() without arguments handles multiple spaces and leading/trailing spaces correctly.\n        raw_tokens = trimmed_music.split()\n        \n        tokens_with_positions: List[Tuple[str, int]] = []\n        for i, raw_token in enumerate(raw_tokens):\n            normalized_t = normalize_token(raw_token)\n            if normalized_t: # Ensure no empty string tokens are added after normalization\n                tokens_with_positions.append((normalized_t, i))\n        \n        return tokens_with_positions\n\n# src/musicparser/parser.py\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\nfrom .config import NOTE_TO_BEATS\nfrom .exceptions import ParseError\nfrom .models import Note # Note model is available but not strictly required for current mapping.\n\nclass MusicParser:\n    \"\"\"Core parser responsible for mapping music tokens to beat durations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        pass\n\n    def parse(self, tokens: List[Tuple[str, int]]) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Converts a list of (token, position) pairs into a list of integer beat durations.\n        Raises ParseError if any token is unrecognized.\n        \"\"\"\n        result_beats: List[int] = []\n        for token, pos in tokens:\n            beat_value = self._map_token(token, pos)\n            result_beats.append(beat_value)\n        return result_beats\n\n    def _map_token(self, token: str, position: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Looks up the beat value for a single token.\n        Raises ParseError if the token is not recognized.\n        \"\"\"\n        if token not in NOTE_TO_BEATS:\n            raise ParseError(f\"Unrecognized token '{token}' found at position {position}.\",\n                             token=token, position=position)\n        return NOTE_TO_BEATS[token]\n\n# src/musicparser/services.py\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n\nfrom .tokenizer import Tokenizer\nfrom .parser import MusicParser\nfrom .exceptions import ParseError\nfrom .config import SUPPORTED_TOKENS\n\nclass ParserService:\n    \"\"\"Public API for parsing music notation, orchestrating tokenization and parsing.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, parser: Optional[MusicParser] = None, tokenizer: Optional[Tokenizer] = None) -> None:\n        self.parser = parser or MusicParser()\n        self.tokenizer = tokenizer or Tokenizer()\n\n    def parse_music(self, music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses a musical notation string into a list of integer beat durations.\n        Raises ParseError for any invalid input.\n        \"\"\"\n        tokens = self.tokenizer.tokenize(music_string)\n        self.validate(tokens) # Perform any additional service-level validation\n        return self.parser.parse(tokens)\n\n    def validate(self, tokens: List[Tuple[str, int]]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Performs lightweight validation on the token list.\n        This method serves as a hook for future higher-level validation rules.\n        \"\"\"\n        for token, pos in tokens:\n            if not token: # Should be handled by tokenizer, but extra check is harmless\n                raise ParseError(f\"Encountered an unexpected empty token at position {pos}.\", token=token, position=pos)\n        pass # Actual token content validation is handled by MusicParser._map_token.\n\n# src/musicparser/cli.py\nimport sys\nimport json\nimport argparse\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .services import ParserService\nfrom .exceptions import ParseError\nfrom .config import VERSION\n\nclass CLI:\n    \"\"\"Command-line interface for the music parser library.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: Optional[ParserService] = None) -> None:\n        self.service = service or ParserService()\n\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the CLI logic, parsing input and printing results or errors.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"music-parse\",\n            description=\"Parse simple ASCII musical notation into beat lengths.\",\n            epilog=\"Example: music-parse 'o o| .|' or echo 'o o|' | music-parse\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"music_string\",\n            nargs=\"?\",  # Positional argument, optional\n            help=\"The musical notation string to parse. If omitted, input is read from stdin.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"-v\", \"--version\", action=\"version\", version=f\"%(prog)s {VERSION}\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        input_str: str\n        if args.music_string:\n            input_str = args.music_string\n        else:\n            if sys.stdin.isatty():\n                print(\"Enter musical notation (e.g., 'o o| .|') and press Ctrl+D (EOF):\", file=sys.stderr)\n            input_str = sys.stdin.read()\n            if not input_str.strip() and not sys.stdin.isatty():\n                # For empty piped input, treat as empty string. parse_music will return [].\n                pass\n\n        try:\n            beats = self.service.parse_music(input_str)\n            self._print_output(beats)\n            return 0\n        except ParseError as e:\n            token_info = f\" (token='{e.token}', position={e.position})\" if e.token is not None else \"\"\n            print(f\"Error: ParseError: {e.message}{token_info}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Error: An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n\n    def _print_output(self, beats: List[int]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Prints the list of beats as a JSON array to stdout.\"\"\"\n        json.dump(beats, sys.stdout)\n        sys.stdout.write(\"\\n\") # Add newline for cleaner terminal output\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the music-parse CLI command.\"\"\"\n    cli = CLI()\n    return cli.run()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n# pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"musicparser\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nauthors = [\n  { name=\"Your Name\", email=\"you@example.com\" },\n]\ndescription = \"A simple Python library and CLI for parsing ASCII musical notation.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.10\"\nkeywords = [\"music\", \"notation\", \"parser\", \"cli\"]\nlicense = { file = \"LICENSE\" }\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules\",\n    \"Topic :: Multimedia :: Sound/Audio\"\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/musicparser\"\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/yourusername/musicparser/issues\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nmusic-parse = \"musicparser.cli:main\"\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ntest = [\"pytest>=7.0\"]\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n\n# README.md\n# Music Parser\n\nA simple Python library and command-line tool to parse ASCII musical notation strings into beat durations.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install musicparser\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom musicparser import parse_music, ParseError\n\ntry:\n    beats = parse_music(\"o o| .| o| o| .| .| .| .| o o\")\n    print(beats)  # Output: [4, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 4]\n\n    beats_empty = parse_music(\"\")\n    print(beats_empty) # Output: []\n\n    beats_invalid = parse_music(\"o x .|\")\nexcept ParseError as e:\n    print(f\"Parsing error: {e.message} (token='{e.token}', position={e.position})\")\n    # Example Output: Parsing error: Unrecognized token 'x' found at position 1. (token='x', position=1)\n```\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\n```bash\n# Parse a string directly\nmusic-parse \"o o| .|\"\n# Output: [4,2,1]\n\n# Parse from piped input\necho \"o o| .| o\" | music-parse\n# Output: [4,2,1,4]\n\n# Get version\nmusic-parse --version\n\n# Handle invalid input\nmusic-parse \"o x .|\"\n# Output (to stderr): Error: ParseError: Unrecognized token 'x' found at position 1. (token='x', position=1)\n# Exit code: 1\n```\n\n## Notation Legend\n\n- `'o'` - whole note, lasts four beats\n- `'o|'` - half note, lasts two beats\n- `'.|'` - quarter note, lasts one beat\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Python 3.10+\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/musicparser.git\ncd musicparser\npip install -e .[test]\npytest\n```\n\n# LICENSE\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) [Year] [Your Name]\n\nPermission is hereby granted, f