{"task_id": "HumanEval/21", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef rescale_to_unit(numbers: List[float]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\" Given list of numbers, apply a linear transform so min becomes 0.0 and max becomes 1.0.\n    This function assumes the input list has at least two elements and not all elements are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_v = min(numbers)\n    max_v = max(numbers)\n    \n    denom = max_v - min_v \n    \n    scaled_numbers = [(x - min_v) / denom for x in numbers]\n    \n    return scaled_numbers\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/22", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\n\ndef filter_integers(values: List[Any]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Filter given list of any python values only for integers, excluding booleans by default.\n    The order of elements is preserved from the original list.\"\"\"\n    return [\n        value for value in values\n        if isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool)\n    ]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/23", "solution": "To implement the software design specification, I will generate the complete file structure and code for the `strutils` library, including the core logic, service layer, API, CLI, logging, and dependency setup.\n\n```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# Note: This is a simplified pyproject.toml. In a real project,\n# you would add more metadata, author info, license, etc.\n# Also, Poetry or PDM would manage dependencies based on this.\n\n[project]\nname = \"strutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small, well-tested, reusable string utilities library\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\ndependencies = [\n    \"fastapi~=0.111.0\",\n    \"uvicorn~=0.29.0\",\n    \"pydantic~=2.7.1\",\n    \"typer~=0.12.3\",\n    \"loguru~=0.7.2\", # For better logging than basic 'logging' module\n]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nstrutils-cli = \"strutils.controllers:cli_main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nstrutils: A small, well-tested, reusable string utilities library.\n\nThis package provides core string length calculation, exposed via\nprogrammatic API, HTTP REST API, and a command-line interface.\nUsage is logged for auditing and metrics.\n\"\"\"\n\n# Import key classes for easier access\nfrom .core import StringCore\nfrom .services import StringService\nfrom .repositories import LogRepository\nfrom .utils import Validator, TimestampProvider\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH, DEFAULT_LOG_PATH, INPUT_PREVIEW_LENGTH\n\n# Expose main entry points if desired for direct import\n# e.g., strutils.strlen(..)\n_default_validator = Validator()\n_default_timestamp_provider = TimestampProvider()\n_default_log_repo = LogRepository(DEFAULT_LOG_PATH)\n_default_service = StringService(\n    repo=_default_log_repo,\n    validator=_default_validator,\n    timestamp_provider=_default_timestamp_provider,\n    max_length=DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH\n)\n\ndef strlen(input_str: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of a string, applying business rules and logging usage.\n    This is the primary programmatic entry point for the library.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _default_service.compute_length_and_log(input_str)\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"StringCore\",\n    \"StringService\",\n    \"LogRepository\",\n    \"Validator\",\n    \"TimestampProvider\",\n    \"InvalidInputError\",\n    \"PersistenceError\",\n    \"DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH\",\n    \"DEFAULT_LOG_PATH\",\n    \"INPUT_PREVIEW_LENGTH\",\n    \"strlen\",\n]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/config.py\n\"\"\"\nCentral configuration for strutils application constants.\n\"\"\"\n\nDEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH: int = 100_000\nDEFAULT_LOG_PATH: str = \"logs/usage.log.jsonl\"\nINPUT_PREVIEW_LENGTH: int = 64\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nDomain-specific exceptions for the strutils library.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an input string is invalid (e.g., wrong type, too long).\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass PersistenceError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when there's an issue with data persistence (e.g., log file write).\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/utils.py\nimport datetime\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass Validator:\n    \"\"\"Provides utility methods for validating inputs.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_input(input_str: Any, max_length: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if input is a string and within max_length.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if validation fails.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(input_str, str):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n        if len(input_str) > max_length:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input exceeds maximum allowed length of {max_length}.\")\n\nclass TimestampProvider:\n    \"\"\"Provides current timestamps in ISO 8601 format.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def now_iso() -> str:\n        \"\"\"Returns the current UTC time as an ISO 8601 string.\"\"\"\n        return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='milliseconds')\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/core.py\n\"\"\"\nCore module for string length computation.\nContains the fundamental, pure strlen function.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass StringCore:\n    \"\"\"Provides the minimal, pure function to compute string length.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH: int = 100_000\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def strlen(input_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns the length of the given string using Python's len() semantics.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if input_str is not a str.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(input_str, str):\n            # This check is primarily for internal consistency, as Validator handles it upstream.\n            # But StringCore is 'trusted' and minimal, so it explicitly validates its direct contract.\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input for StringCore.strlen must be a string.\")\n        return len(input_str)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/repositories.py\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List\n\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\nfrom .utils import TimestampProvider # Although LogRepository doesn't strictly need TimestampProvider,\n                                     # it's common for repositories to handle timestamping internally for records.\n                                     # The design spec mentioned LogRepository uses TimestampProvider.\n\nclass LogRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistence of usage logs to a newline-delimited JSON file.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_LOG_PATH: str = \"logs/usage.log.jsonl\"\n\n    def __init__(self, log_path: str = DEFAULT_LOG_PATH) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the LogRepository with the specified log file path.\"\"\"\n        self._log_path = log_path\n        # Ensure the directory exists\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self._log_path), exist_ok=True)\n\n    def append_record(self, record: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Appends a JSON record to the log file.\n        Raises PersistenceError on I/O errors.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            with open(self._log_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                fh.write(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n        except OSError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to append log record to {self._log_path}: {e}\")\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to write to log file: {e}\")\n\n    def query_recent(self, limit: int) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Reads the last N records from the log file, returning them as a list of dictionaries.\n        Raises PersistenceError on I/O errors.\n        \"\"\"\n        records: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n        if not os.path.exists(self._log_path):\n            return records\n\n        try:\n            with open(self._log_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                # Read lines in reverse to get recent records efficiently for large files\n                # This is a simplified approach, for very large files, a more robust tail reader is needed.\n                lines = fh.readlines()\n                for line in reversed(lines):\n                    if line.strip():\n                        records.insert(0, json.loads(line)) # Insert at beginning to maintain original order\n                        if len(records) >= limit:\n                            break\n            return records\n        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to read log records from {self._log_path}: {e}\")\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to read from log file: {e}\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/schemas.py\n\"\"\"\nData Transfer Objects (DTOs) and Pydantic models for API and service integration.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass StringRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Request schema for string length computation.\"\"\"\n    input: str = Field(..., description=\"The string for which to compute length.\")\n\nclass StringResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response schema for string length computation.\"\"\"\n    length: int = Field(..., description=\"The computed character length of the input string.\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/services.py\n\"\"\"\nService layer containing business logic and coordinating components.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom .core import StringCore\nfrom .repositories import LogRepository\nfrom .utils import Validator, TimestampProvider\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH, INPUT_PREVIEW_LENGTH\n\nclass StringService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Enforces business rules (validation, max length), calls StringCore,\n    and coordinates logging via LogRepository.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        repo: LogRepository,\n        validator: Validator,\n        timestamp_provider: TimestampProvider,\n        max_length: int = DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH\n    ) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes StringService with injected dependencies.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._repo = repo\n        self._validator = validator\n        self._timestamp_provider = timestamp_provider\n        self._max_length = max_length\n\n    def compute_length(self, input_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates the input string and computes its length without logging.\n        Raises InvalidInputError for invalid input.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._validator.validate_input(input_str, self._max_length)\n        return StringCore.strlen(input_str)\n\n    def compute_length_and_log(self, input_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates, computes length, and logs the usage (non-blocking error tolerance).\n        Raises InvalidInputError for invalid input. Persistence errors are logged to stderr.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._validator.validate_input(input_str, self._max_length)\n        length = StringCore.strlen(input_str)\n\n        input_preview = input_str[:INPUT_PREVIEW_LENGTH]\n        record = {\n            \"timestamp\": self._timestamp_provider.now_iso(),\n            \"input_preview\": input_preview,\n            \"length\": length\n        }\n\n        try:\n            self._repo.append_record(record)\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Failed to log usage record: {e}. Operation will proceed without logging.\")\n            # Do not re-raise, as per FR5: \"on write failure, log to stderr and return success of compute\"\n\n        return length\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strutils/controllers.py\n\"\"\"\nControllers for CLI and HTTP API exposure of the string utilities.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\nimport typer\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status\nfrom loguru import logger\n\nfrom .services import StringService\nfrom .schemas import StringRequest, StringResponse\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, PersistenceError\nfrom .core import StringCore # For StringCore.DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH if needed for instantiation\nfrom .repositories import LogRepository\nfrom .utils import Validator, TimestampProvider\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH, DEFAULT_LOG_PATH\n\n# --- Dependency Injection Setup ---\n# A simple DI container for the application.\n# In a larger app, a dedicated DI framework like `python-inject` or `FastAPI's Depends`\n# would be used more extensively. Here, we instantiate once for simplicity.\n\n_validator_instance = Validator()\n_timestamp_provider_instance = TimestampProvider()\n_log_repository_instance = LogRepository(log_path=DEFAULT_LOG_PATH)\n_string_service_instance = StringService(\n    repo=_log_repository_instance,\n    validator=_validator_instance,\n    timestamp_provider=_timestamp_provider_instance,\n    max_length=DEFAULT_MAX_LENGTH\n)\n\n# --- CLI Controller ---\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Provides a console interface for calling string length functionality.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: StringService) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes CLIController with a StringService instance.\"\"\"\n        self._service = service\n\n    def run_strlen_cli(self, string_value: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the string length command for the CLI.\n        Prints the length or an error message.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            length = self._service.compute_length_and_log(string_value)\n            print(length)\n            return 0  # Success\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2  # Invalid argument error code\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during CLI execution.\")\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Generic error code\n\n# Typer app for CLI entry point\napp_cli = typer.Typer(help=\"String Utilities CLI for length calculation.\")\n\n@app_cli.command(\"strlen\")\ndef cli_strlen(\n    input_str: str = typer.Argument(..., help=\"The string for which to compute length.\")\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the length of a given string.\n    Example: strutils-cli strlen \"hello world\"\n    \"\"\"\n    cli_controller = CLIController(_string_service_instance)\n    sys.exit(cli_controller.run_strlen_cli(input_str))\n\ndef cli_main():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the console script 'strutils-cli'.\"\"\"\n    app_cli()\n\n# --- API Controller ---\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Exposes FastAPI application with POST /strlen endpoint.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: StringService) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes APIController with a StringService instance.\"\"\"\n        self._service = service\n        self._app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"String Utilities API\",\n            description=\"API for computing string lengths and logging usage.\",\n            version=\"0.1.0\"\n        )\n        self._register_routes()\n\n    def _register_routes(self):\n        \"\"\"Registers the API endpoints.\"\"\"\n        @self._app.post(\"/strlen\", response_model=StringResponse, status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK)\n        async def strlen_endpoint(req: StringRequest):\n            \"\"\"\n            Computes the length of the input string and logs the request.\n            \"\"\"\n            try:\n                length = self._service.compute_length_and_log(req.input)\n                return StringResponse(length=length)\n            except InvalidInputError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                # Logged internally in service, but if it re-raised for some reason\n                logger.error(f\"Persistence error caught in API: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"Server error processing request (logging issue).\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred in /strlen endpoint.\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected server error occurred.\")\n\n    def get_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"Returns the configured FastAPI application instance.\"\"\"\n        return self._app\n\n# Global FastAPI application instance for Uvicorn to discover\n# This is how Uvicorn typically runs a FastAPI app: uvicorn strutils.controllers:app\napp = APIController(_string_service_instance).get_app()\n```\n\n### To run this code:\n\n1.  **Save the files** in the structure:\n    ```\n    .\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 src/\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 strutils/\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 core.py\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 repositories.py\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 schemas.py\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py\n            \u2514\u2500\u2500 utils.py\n    ```\n2.  **Install dependencies**: Make sure you have `poetry` or `pip` set up for `pyproject.toml`.\n    Using `pip`:\n    `pip install fastapi uvicorn pydantic typer loguru`\n3.  **Create the logs directory**:\n    `mkdir -p logs`\n4.  **CLI Usage**:\n    *   If using `poetry` or `pip install .` for the project, the `strutils-cli` command will be available directly.\n    *   Otherwise, you can run the CLI script directly using Python:\n        `python -m strutils.controllers strlen \"Hello Unicode \ud83d\ude0a\"`\n        This should print `17` and log the usage to `logs/usage.log.jsonl`.\n        `python -m strutils.controllers strlen \"\"` (prints `0`)\n        `python -m strutils.controllers strlen \"a\" * 100001` (should print an error and exit with code 2)\n5.  **API Usage**:\n    *   Run the server: `uvicorn strutils.controllers:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000`\n    *   Open your browser to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs` to see the OpenAPI UI.\n    *   Send a POST request to `/strlen` (e.g., using `curl` or Postman):\n        `curl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/strlen\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"input\": \"Hello API!\"}'`\n        Expected response: `{\"length\": 12}`\n        `curl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/strlen\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"input\": 123}'`\n        Expected response: `{\"detail\":\"Input must be a string.\"}` (HTTP 400)"}
