{"task_id": "HumanEval/29", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# This file is used by build tools like Poetry to manage project metadata and dependencies.\n# It adheres to PEP 621.\n[project]\nname = \"strfilter\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python library for filtering lists of strings by a prefix.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules\",\n    \"Topic :: Text Processing\",\n]\n\n[project.dependencies]\n# Core library has no external dependencies\n# For API, 'flask' is an optional dependency, specified in [project.optional-dependencies.api]\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\napi = [\n    \"flask>=2.0.0\",\n]\ntest = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0.0\",\n    \"pytest-cov>=4.0.0\",\n]\n\n[project.scripts]\nstrfilter = \"strfilter.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n```\n```python\n# README.md\n# strfilter\n\nA reliable, well-tested Python library and small runtime for filtering lists of strings by a prefix.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Programmatic API**: Use `filter_by_prefix` directly in your Python code.\n- **Command-Line Interface (CLI)**: Filter strings from an inline list or a file.\n- **Optional HTTP API**: An optional Flask-based HTTP endpoint for filtering.\n- **Extensible Repositories**: Easily extend to support other string sources.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install strfilter\n```\n\nTo install with HTTP API support (requires Flask):\n```bash\npip install \"strfilter[api]\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom strfilter import FilterService, InMemoryStringRepository, FileStringRepository\n\n# Basic filtering\nstrings = [\"apple\", \"apricot\", \"banana\", \"grape\"]\nfiltered = FilterService().filter_by_prefix(\"ap\", strings)\nprint(filtered) # Output: ['apple', 'apricot']\n\n# Using an in-memory repository\nrepo = InMemoryStringRepository([\"cat\", \"car\", \"dog\"])\nsvc = FilterService(repository=repo)\nfiltered_repo = svc.filter_by_prefix(\"c\")\nprint(filtered_repo) # Output: ['cat', 'car']\n\n# Using a file repository\n# Assuming you have a file named 'my_strings.txt' with:\n# apple\n# apricot\n# banana\n#\n# repo = FileStringRepository(\"my_strings.txt\")\n# svc = FilterService(repository=repo)\n# filtered_file = svc.filter_by_prefix(\"ap\")\n# print(filtered_file) # Output: ['apple', 'apricot']\n```\n\n### CLI\n\nFilter from a comma-separated list:\n```bash\nstrfilter --prefix \"a\" --list \"apple,apricot,banana,grape\"\n# Output: [\"apple\", \"apricot\"]\n```\n\nFilter from a file (assuming `my_strings.txt` exists with newline-separated strings):\n```bash\nstrfilter --prefix \"ap\" --file my_strings.txt\n# Output: [\"apple\", \"apricot\"]\n```\n\n### HTTP API (Optional)\n\nFirst, install with the `api` extra: `pip install \"strfilter[api]\"`.\n\nYou can run the API using a WSGI server (e.g., Gunicorn, Flask's development server):\n\n```python\n# app_server.py\nfrom strfilter.app import create_app\n\napp = create_app()\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    app.run(debug=True, port=5000)\n```\n\nThen run `python app_server.py`.\n\nOnce the server is running, you can make POST requests:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"prefix\": \"ap\", \"strings\": [\"apple\", \"apricot\", \"banana\"]}' \\\n     http://127.0.0.1:5000/filter\n# Output: {\"filtered\": [\"apple\", \"apricot\"]}\n```\n\nIf you start the server with a pre-configured repository (e.g., `create_app(repository=FileStringRepository(\"my_strings.txt\"))`), you can omit the `strings` field in the request:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"prefix\": \"ap\"}' \\\n     http://127.0.0.1:5000/filter\n# Output: {\"filtered\": [\"apple\", \"apricot\"]} (based on 'my_strings.txt')\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Setup\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/your/strfilter.git\ncd strfilter\npip install poetry # If you don't have poetry\npoetry install --with dev,api\npoetry shell\n```\n\n### Running Tests\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n## Contributing\nContributions are welcome! Please open issues or pull requests on the GitHub repository.\n\n## License\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License.\n```\n```python\n# setup.cfg\n[tool:pytest]\n# Add any pytest specific configuration here\n# For example, to add markers or change test discovery\ntestpaths = tests\npython_files = test_*.py\naddopts = --cov=strfilter --cov-report=term-missing --strict-markers\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nstrfilter - A library for prefix filtering strings.\n\"\"\"\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, RepositoryError\nfrom .repository import StringRepository, InMemoryStringRepository, FileStringRepository\nfrom .service import FilterService\nfrom .cli import main as cli_main\nfrom .app import create_app as create_api_app\n\n# Expose key components directly for easier import\n__all__ = [\n    \"__version__\",\n    \"ValidationError\",\n    \"RepositoryError\",\n    \"StringRepository\",\n    \"InMemoryStringRepository\",\n    \"FileStringRepository\",\n    \"FilterService\",\n    \"cli_main\",\n    \"create_api_app\",\n]\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FilterRequest:\n    \"\"\"Data model for a filter request.\"\"\"\n    prefix: str\n    strings: List[str]\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, data: dict) -> \"FilterRequest\":\n        \"\"\"Create FilterRequest from dictionary, validating types.\"\"\"\n        prefix = data.get(\"prefix\")\n        strings = data.get(\"strings\")\n\n        if not isinstance(prefix, str):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Prefix must be a string.\")\n        if strings is not None and (not isinstance(strings, list) or any(not isinstance(s, str) for s in strings)):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Strings must be a list of strings or null.\")\n\n        # If strings is None, default to an empty list for consistency in the model\n        # The service layer will then decide whether to use a repository.\n        return cls(prefix=prefix, strings=strings if strings is not None else [])\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FilterResult:\n    \"\"\"Data model for a filter result.\"\"\"\n    filtered: List[str]\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Serialize FilterResult to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"filtered\": self.filtered}\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/exceptions.py\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception for invalid user input or type errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass RepositoryError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception for issues with data repositories.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/repository.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional, Protocol, runtime_checkable\nimport os\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, RepositoryError\n\n@runtime_checkable\nclass StringRepository(Protocol):\n    \"\"\"Protocol for string repositories.\"\"\"\n    def get_all(self) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieve all strings from the repository.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\nclass InMemoryStringRepository:\n    \"\"\"An in-memory repository for strings.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, strings: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> None:\n        if strings is not None and (not isinstance(strings, list) or any(not isinstance(s, str) for s in strings)):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Initial strings must be List[str] or None.\")\n        self._strings: List[str] = list(strings) if strings else []\n\n    def get_all(self) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a shallow copy of the stored strings.\"\"\"\n        return list(self._strings)\n\n    def add(self, strings: List[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Adds strings to the repository.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(strings, list) or any(not isinstance(s, str) for s in strings):\n            raise ValidationError(\"add expects List[str].\")\n        self._strings.extend(strings)\n\nclass FileStringRepository:\n    \"\"\"A repository that loads strings from a newline-delimited text file.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, path: str, encoding: str = \"utf-8\") -> None:\n        if not isinstance(path, str):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Path must be a string.\")\n        self._path: str = path\n        self._encoding: str = encoding\n\n    def get_all(self) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Reads and returns lines from the file.\"\"\"\n        if not os.path.exists(self._path):\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"File not found: {self._path}\")\n        try:\n            with open(self._path, \"r\", encoding=self._encoding) as f:\n                lines = [line.strip() for line in f]\n            return lines\n        except OSError as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to read file {self._path}: {e}\") from e\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/service.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, RepositoryError\nfrom .repository import StringRepository\nfrom .utils import validate_prefix # pylint: disable=W0611\n\nclass FilterService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Business logic for filtering strings by a prefix.\n    Supports explicit string lists or an injected repository.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repository: Optional[StringRepository] = None) -> None:\n        self._repository: Optional[StringRepository] = repository\n\n    def filter_by_prefix(self, prefix: str, strings: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Filters a list of strings by a given prefix.\n        If strings are not provided, it attempts to use the configured repository.\n        \"\"\"\n        validate_prefix(prefix) # Ensure prefix is a string.\n\n        source_list = strings\n        if source_list is None:\n            if not self._repository:\n                raise ValidationError(\"No source strings provided and no repository configured.\")\n            try:\n                source_list = self._repository.get_all()\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise RepositoryError(\"Failed to load strings from repository.\") from e\n\n        if not isinstance(source_list, list) or any(not isinstance(s, str) for s in source_list):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Source must be a List[str].\")\n\n        if prefix == \"\":\n            return list(source_list) # Return a copy if prefix is empty.\n\n        return [s for s in source_list if s.startswith(prefix)]\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/utils.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\ndef validate_prefix(prefix: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates that the prefix is a string.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(prefix, str):\n        raise ValidationError(\"Prefix must be a string.\")\n\ndef parse_list_arg(list_arg: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Parses a comma-separated string into a list of strings.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_arg, str):\n        raise ValidationError(\"List argument must be a string.\")\n    if not list_arg.strip():\n        return []\n    return [s.strip() for s in list_arg.split(',')]\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/controller.py\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .service import FilterService\nfrom .repository import FileStringRepository, InMemoryStringRepository\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, RepositoryError\nfrom .utils import parse_list_arg\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles command-line interface interactions, parsing arguments,\n    and invoking the FilterService.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: FilterService) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses CLI arguments, performs filtering, and prints results to stdout.\n        Returns 0 on success, non-zero on error.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog='strfilter',\n            description='Filter lists of strings by a prefix.'\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            '--prefix',\n            required=True,\n            help='The prefix to filter by.'\n        )\n        group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n        group.add_argument(\n            '--list',\n            help='A comma-separated list of strings to filter.'\n        )\n        group.add_argument(\n            '--file',\n            help='Path to a newline-delimited file containing strings to filter.'\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        try:\n            result_list: List[str]\n\n            if args.list is not None:\n                strings = parse_list_arg(args.list)\n                result_list = self.service.filter_by_prefix(args.prefix, strings=strings)\n            elif args.file is not None:\n                # When using --file, we create a new service instance with a FileStringRepository\n                # to allow the service to fetch strings from the file.\n                file_repo = FileStringRepository(args.file)\n                file_service = FilterService(repository=file_repo)\n                result_list = file_service.filter_by_prefix(args.prefix)\n            else: # Should not happen due to mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n                raise ValidationError(\"Either --list or --file must be provided.\")\n\n            print(json.dumps(result_list))\n            return 0\n        except (ValidationError, RepositoryError) as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/api.py\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\nfrom .service import FilterService\nfrom .models import FilterRequest, FilterResult\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, RepositoryError\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from flask import Flask, Request, jsonify, request\n\nclass ApiController:\n    \"\"\"\n    HTTP API controller for filtering strings using Flask.\n    This component is designed to be optional, requiring Flask to be installed.\n    \"\"\"\n    API_ROUTE = \"/filter\"\n\n    def __init__(self, service: FilterService) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n\n    def create_app(self) -> \"Flask\":\n        \"\"\"\n        Creates and configures a Flask application with the /filter endpoint.\n        Raises RuntimeError if Flask is not installed.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            from flask import Flask, request, jsonify\n        except ImportError as e:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Flask is not installed. Install with `pip install strfilter[api]` to use the HTTP API.\") from e\n\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n\n        @app.route(self.API_ROUTE, methods=[\"POST\"])\n        def filter_endpoint():\n            if not request.is_json:\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"Request must be JSON\"}), 400\n\n            try:\n                data = request.get_json()\n                if data is None:\n                    return jsonify({\"error\": \"Invalid JSON payload\"}), 400\n\n                # Validate data and create a FilterRequest model\n                req = FilterRequest.from_dict(data)\n\n                # Call the service. If req.strings is empty, the service will attempt\n                # to use its injected repository if available.\n                filtered_strings = self.service.filter_by_prefix(\n                    prefix=req.prefix,\n                    strings=req.strings if req.strings else None\n                )\n                result = FilterResult(filtered=filtered_strings)\n                return jsonify(result.to_dict()), 200\n\n            except ValidationError as e:\n                return jsonify({\"error\": str(e)}), 400\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                # Repository errors are typically 500s unless they are client-induced (e.g., file not found specified in config)\n                return jsonify({\"error\": f\"Repository error: {e}\"}), 500\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Catch any other unexpected errors\n                return jsonify({\"error\": f\"An internal server error occurred: {e}\"}), 500\n        return app\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/cli.py\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom .service import FilterService\nfrom .controller import CLIController\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the CLI application.\n    Instantiates FilterService and CLIController, then runs the CLI.\n    \"\"\"\n    # For CLI, we generally start with a FilterService without a default repository\n    # as the source (list or file) is specified per command.\n    service = FilterService()\n    controller = CLIController(service)\n    return controller.run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # This block is for direct script execution, e.g., `python -m strfilter.cli`\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n```python\n# src/strfilter/app.py\nfrom typing import Optional, TYPE_CHECKING\nfrom .service import FilterService\nfrom .repository import StringRepository\nfrom .api import ApiController\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from flask import Flask\n\ndef create_app(repository: Optional[StringRepository] = None) -> \"Flask\":\n    \"\"\"\n    Application factory for the HTTP API.\n    Creates and configures a Flask app with the FilterService.\n    An optional repository can be provided to the FilterService\n    for cases where the API expects a default data source.\n    \"\"\"\n    filter_service = FilterService(repository=repository)\n    api_controller = ApiController(service=filter_service)\n    return api_controller.create_app()\n```"}
