{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_third([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_third([5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2])\n    [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a shallow copy of the list to avoid modifying the original\n    result = list(l)\n\n    # Collect elements at indices divisible by 3\n    extracted_elements = []\n    divisible_by_3_indices = []\n    for i in range(len(result)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            divisible_by_3_indices.append(i)\n            extracted_elements.append(result[i])\n\n    # Sort the collected elements\n    extracted_elements.sort()\n\n    # Place the sorted elements back into the result list at their original indices\n    for i, val in zip(divisible_by_3_indices, extracted_elements):\n        result[i] = val\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/34", "solution": "```\npyproject.toml\n```toml\n[project]\nname = \"uniqutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python utility for returning sorted unique elements from a list.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <your.email@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\ndependencies = []\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/uniqutils\"\nRepository = \"https://github.com/yourusername/uniqutils\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nuniqutils = \"uniqutils.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n```\n\nREADME.md\n```markdown\n# UniqUtils\n\nA Python utility that provides a function and a command-line tool to deduplicate and sort elements from lists or iterables.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install uniqutils\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Python API\n\n```python\nfrom uniqutils import unique\n\n# Basic usage: unique and sorted\ndata = [5, 3, 5, 2, 3, 3, 9, 0, 123]\nresult = unique(data)\n# result will be [0, 2, 3, 5, 9, 123]\n\n# Preserve original order\ndata = [3, 1, 2, 3, 2]\nresult_preserved = unique(data, preserve_order=True)\n# result_preserved will be [3, 1, 2]\n\n# Using a key function for uniqueness and sorting\nitems = [{'id': 1, 'name': 'apple'}, {'id': 2, 'name': 'banana'}, {'id': 1, 'name': 'Apple'}]\nresult_keyed = unique(items, key=lambda x: x['id'])\n# result_keyed will be [{'id': 1, 'name': 'apple'}, {'id': 2, 'name': 'banana'}] (order might vary based on stable sort)\n\n# With unhashable items and preserving order\nunhashable_items = [[1,2], [3,4], [1,2], [5,6]]\nresult_unhashable = unique(unhashable_items, preserve_order=True)\n# result_unhashable will be [[1,2], [3,4], [5,6]]\n```\n\n### Command Line Interface (CLI)\n\nYou can use the `uniqutils` command directly:\n\n```bash\n# Read from stdin (whitespace separated)\necho \"5 3 5 2 3 3 9 0 123\" | uniqutils unique\n# Output:\n# 0\n# 2\n# 3\n# 5\n# 9\n# 123\n\n# Preserve order\necho \"3 1 2 3 2\" | uniqutils unique --preserve-order\n# Output:\n# 3\n# 1\n# 2\n\n# Read from a file (newline or whitespace separated)\n# Assuming 'data.txt' contains:\n# apple\n# banana\n# apple\nuniqutils unique -i data.txt\n# Output:\n# apple\n# banana\n\n# Using a key function (importable path to a callable)\n# Example: create a file `my_keys.py`:\n# def item_id(item_str):\n#     import json\n#     return json.loads(item_str)['id']\n#\n# Then, use:\n# echo '{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"A\"}\\n{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"B\"}\\n{\"id\":1,\"name\":\"C\"}' | uniqutils unique --key my_keys.item_id\n```\n\n## Development\n\nSee the source code for detailed architecture and design.\n```\n\nsrc/uniqutils/__init__.py\n```python\nfrom typing import Iterable, Any, Callable, List, Optional\nfrom .unique_service import UniqueService\nfrom .exceptions import UniqueError\n\n# Expose the primary function for package users.\ndef unique(items: Iterable[Any], preserve_order: bool = False, key: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Return sorted unique elements in a list, with options for order preservation and custom key.\n    This is the main public API function.\n    \"\"\"\n    service = UniqueService()\n    return service.deduplicate(items, preserve_order=preserve_order, key=key)\n\n__all__ = [\"unique\", \"UniqueError\"]\n```\n\nsrc/uniqutils/unique_service.py\n```python\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Iterable, List, Optional\n\nfrom .exceptions import UniqueError\nfrom .strategies import HashSetStrategy, SortStrategy, StableOrderStrategy, UniqueStrategy\nfrom .utils import is_hashable, normalize_iterable\n\n\nclass UniqueService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates deduplication by selecting the appropriate strategy.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._logger = logging.getLogger(\"uniqutils.UniqueService\")\n\n    def deduplicate(\n        self,\n        items: Iterable[Any],\n        preserve_order: bool = False,\n        key: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None,\n    ) -> List[Any]:\n        \"\"\"Deduplicates items, optionally preserving order or using a key.\"\"\"\n        lst = normalize_iterable(items)\n        if not lst:\n            return []\n\n        strategy = self._select_strategy(lst, preserve_order, key)\n        result = strategy.dedupe(lst, key=key)\n\n        # If strategy didn't ensure sorting and preserve_order is False, sort here.\n        if not preserve_order and not isinstance(strategy, SortStrategy):\n            try:\n                return sorted(result, key=key)\n            except TypeError as e:\n                raise UniqueError(\n                    \"Elements not comparable for sorting; provide a key or set preserve_order=True\"\n                ) from e\n        return result\n\n    def _select_strategy(\n        self, items: Iterable[Any], preserve_order: bool, key: Optional[Callable]\n    ) -> UniqueStrategy:\n        \"\"\"Selects the best deduplication strategy based on inputs.\"\"\"\n        if preserve_order:\n            self._logger.debug(\"Selecting StableOrderStrategy due to preserve_order=True\")\n            return StableOrderStrategy()\n\n        # Heuristic: if all items or their key results are hashable, try HashSetStrategy.\n        try:\n            if all(is_hashable(x if key is None else key(x)) for x in items):\n                self._logger.debug(\"Selecting HashSetStrategy as items are hashable\")\n                return HashSetStrategy()\n        except TypeError:\n            self._logger.debug(\"Fallback to SortStrategy as some items or keys are unhashable.\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            self._logger.debug(f\"Key function raised an error during hashability check: {e}. Falling back to SortStrategy.\")\n\n        self._logger.debug(\"Selecting SortStrategy as a general fallback.\")\n        return SortStrategy()\n\n```\n\nsrc/uniqutils/strategies.py\n```python\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Iterable, List, Optional\n\nfrom .exceptions import UniqueError\nfrom .utils import is_hashable\n\n\nclass UniqueStrategy:\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class for deduplication strategies.\"\"\"\n\n    def dedupe(self, items: Iterable[Any], key: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None) -> List[Any]:\n        \"\"\"Removes duplicate elements from an iterable.\"\"\"\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n\nclass HashSetStrategy(UniqueStrategy):\n    \"\"\"Deduplicates items efficiently using a set for hashable items/keys.\"\"\"\n\n    def dedupe(self, items: Iterable[Any], key: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None) -> List[Any]:\n        seen = set()\n        out = []\n        for it in items:\n            try:\n                k = key(it) if key else it\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise UniqueError(f\"Key function failed for item {it}: {e}\") from e\n\n            try:\n                if k not in seen:\n                    seen.add(k)\n                    out.append(it)\n            except TypeError as e:\n                raise UniqueError(\n                    f\"Unhashable item '{k}' encountered; cannot use HashSetStrategy. \"\n                    \"Ensure items or key results are hashable, or use preserve_order=True.\"\n                ) from e\n        return out\n\n\nclass StableOrderStrategy(UniqueStrategy):\n    \"\"\"Deduplicates items while preserving their original order, supporting unhashable types.\"\"\"\n\n    def dedupe(self, items: Iterable[Any], key: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None) -> List[Any]:\n        seen_keys = []\n        out = []\n        for it in items:\n            try:\n                k = key(it) if key else it\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise UniqueError(f\"Key function failed for item {it}: {e}\") from e\n\n            if not any(k == seen_k for seen_k in seen_keys):\n                seen_keys.append(k)\n                out.append(it)\n        return out\n\n\nclass SortStrategy(UniqueStrategy):\n    \"\"\"Deduplicates items by sorting and then removing adjacent duplicates.\"\"\"\n\n    def dedupe(self, items: Iterable[Any], key: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None) -> List[Any]:\n        lst = list(items)\n        if not lst:\n            return []\n        try:\n            lst.sort(key=key)\n        except TypeError as e:\n            raise UniqueError(\n                \"Cannot sort items; elements are uncomparable. \"\n                \"Provide a key or set preserve_order=True.\"\n            ) from e\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise UniqueError(f\"Sorting failed due to key function: {e}\") from e\n\n        out = [lst[0]]\n        prev_key_val = key(lst[0]) if key else lst[0]\n\n        for it in lst[1:]:\n            current_key_val = key(it) if key else it\n            if current_key_val != prev_key_val:\n                out.append(it)\n                prev_key_val = current_key_val\n        return out\n\n```\n\nsrc/uniqutils/exceptions.py\n```python\nclass UniqueError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for errors within the unique utility.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\n```\n\nsrc/uniqutils/utils.py\n```python\nimport importlib\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Iterable, List\n\nfrom .exceptions import UniqueError\n\n\ndef is_hashable(obj: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an object is hashable.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        hash(obj)\n        return True\n    except TypeError:\n        return False\n\n\ndef import_from_string(path: str) -> Callable:\n    \"\"\"Imports a callable from a dotted module path string.\"\"\"\n    if not path:\n        raise UniqueError(\"Key function path cannot be empty.\")\n    try:\n        module_path, attr = path.rsplit(\".\", 1)\n        module = importlib.import_module(module_path)\n        callable_obj = getattr(module, attr)\n        if not callable(callable_obj):\n            raise TypeError(f\"'{path}' is not a callable object.\")\n        return callable_obj\n    except (ImportError, AttributeError, ValueError, TypeError) as e:\n        raise UniqueError(f\"Could not import key function '{path}': {e}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise UniqueError(f\"An unexpected error occurred importing key function '{path}': {e}\") from e\n\n\ndef normalize_iterable(src: Iterable[Any]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Converts an iterable to a list, raising an error for non-iterables.\"\"\"\n    if src is None:\n        return []\n    try:\n        return list(src)\n    except TypeError as e:\n        raise UniqueError(\"Provided items are not iterable\") from e\n\n```\n\nsrc/uniqutils/cli.py\n```python\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .exceptions import UniqueError\nfrom .unique_service import UniqueService\nfrom .utils import import_from_string, normalize_iterable\n\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line argument parsing, input/output, and interaction with UniqueService.\"\"\"\n\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses arguments, processes input, and prints unique items to stdout.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"uniqutils\", description=\"Utility to get unique, sorted elements from a list.\"\n        )\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(\n            dest=\"cmd\", help=\"Available commands\", required=True\n        )\n\n        unique_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n            \"unique\", help=\"Deduplicate and sort elements.\"\n        )\n        unique_parser.add_argument(\n            \"-p\",\n            \"--preserve-order\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Preserve the original order of elements.\",\n        )\n        unique_parser.add_argument(\n            \"-k\",\n            \"--key\",\n            type=str,\n            default=None,\n            help=\"Dotted import path to a callable key function (e.g., 'mymodule.my_key').\",\n        )\n        unique_parser.add_argument(\n            \"-i\",\n            \"--input\",\n            type=str,\n            default=None,\n            help=\"Path to an input file. Reads from stdin if not provided.\",\n        )\n        unique_parser.add_argument(\n            \"-s\",\n            \"--separator\",\n            type=str,\n            default=None,\n            help=\"Separator for input items (default: whitespace or newline if file).\",\n        )\n        unique_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--debug\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Show full stack trace on unexpected errors.\",\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        try:\n            items: List[Any]\n            if args.input:\n                with open(args.input, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                    if args.separator is None:  # Default to newline separation for files\n                        items = [line.rstrip(\"\\n\") for line in fh if line.strip() != \"\"]\n                    else:  # Custom separator for files\n                        content = fh.read()\n                        items = [s for s in content.split(args.separator) if s.strip() != \"\"]\n            else:\n                stdin_content = sys.stdin.read()\n                if args.separator is None:  # Default to whitespace for stdin\n                    items = [s for s in stdin_content.split() if s.strip() != \"\"]\n                else:  # Custom separator for stdin\n                    items = [s for s in stdin_content.split(args.separator) if s.strip() != \"\"]\n\n            key_fn = import_from_string(args.key) if args.key else None\n\n            svc = UniqueService()\n            result = svc.deduplicate(items, preserve_order=args.preserve_order, key=key_fn)\n\n            for item in result:\n                sys.stdout.write(str(item) + \"\\n\")\n            return 0\n\n        except UniqueError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            if args.debug:\n                import traceback\n                traceback.print_exc(file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    return CLIController().run()\n\n```\n```"}
