{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Returns string representation after the conversion.\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    sign = \"-\" if x < 0 else \"\"\n    n = abs(x)\n    digits = []\n\n    while n > 0:\n        digits.append(str(n % base))\n        n //= base\n\n    return sign + \"\".join(reversed(digits))"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```\npyproject.toml\n```toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"baseconv\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reliable library to convert non-negative integers into string representations in bases < 10.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"baseconv\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.9,<4.0\"\nFlask = { version = \"^3.0.0\", optional = true }\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.0.0\"\n\n[tool.poetry.extras]\nhttp = [\"Flask\"]\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nbaseconv = \"baseconv.__main__:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n```\n\n```python\nREADME.md\n```\n# Base Conversion Library\n\nThis project provides a Python library, CLI tool, and optional HTTP endpoint for converting non-negative integers to their string representation in bases 2 through 9.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Using poetry\npoetry install\npoetry install --with http # For HTTP endpoint functionality\n\n# Or using pip\npip install .\npip install \".[http]\" # For HTTP endpoint functionality\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Python Library\n\n```python\nfrom baseconv import change_base, InvalidInputError, InvalidBaseError\n\ntry:\n    result = change_base(8, 3)\n    print(f\"8 in base 3 is: {result}\") # Output: 8 in base 3 is: 22\n\n    result = change_base(15, 2)\n    print(f\"15 in base 2 is: {result}\") # Output: 15 in base 2 is: 1111\n\n    # Example of invalid input\n    change_base(-5, 2)\nexcept (InvalidInputError, InvalidBaseError) as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\n# Convert 8 to base 3\npoetry run baseconv convert --x 8 --base 3\n# Output: 22\n\n# Convert 15 to base 2\npoetry run baseconv convert --x 15 --base 2\n# Output: 1111\n\n# Example of invalid input\npoetry run baseconv convert --x -5 --base 2\n# Output: Error: Input number must be a non-negative integer. (exit code 2)\n\n# Example of invalid base\npoetry run baseconv convert --x 8 --base 1\n# Output: Error: Base must be an integer between 2 and 9, inclusive. (exit code 3)\n```\n\n### HTTP Endpoint (Optional)\n\nFirst, ensure Flask is installed (`pip install \".[http]\"`).\n\nRun the HTTP server:\n```bash\npython -m baseconv.http_adapter\n# Or using poetry\npoetry run python -m baseconv.http_adapter\n```\nThis will start a Flask development server (e.g., on `http://127.0.0.1:5000`).\n\nThen, you can send POST requests:\n\n```bash\n# Success example\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"x\": 8, \"base\": 3}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/convert\n# Response: {\"result\":\"22\"}\n\n# Error example\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"x\": -1, \"base\": 2}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/convert\n# Response: {\"error\":\"Input number must be a non-negative integer.\"}\n```\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/__init__.py\n```\nfrom .core import BaseConverter\nfrom .validator import ValidationService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidBaseError, InvalidInputError\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Returns string representation after the conversion.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a new BaseConverter for each call to ensure statelessness\n    # and provide default validator if none is explicitly set.\n    return BaseConverter().convert(x, base)\n\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/core.py\n```\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nfrom .validator import ValidationService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, InvalidBaseError\n\nclass BaseConverter:\n    \"\"\"Core logic for converting non-negative integers to a string representation in a given base.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, validator: Optional[ValidationService] = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Constructs a BaseConverter, optionally with an injected ValidationService.\"\"\"\n        self._validator = validator if validator is not None else ValidationService()\n\n    def convert(self, x: int, base: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Public API for conversion. Validates inputs and returns the base-b string.\"\"\"\n        self._validator.validate(x, base)\n        if x == 0:\n            return \"0\"\n        return self._convert_positive(x, base)\n\n    def _convert_positive(self, x: int, base: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Internal routine to convert a positive integer to its base-b string.\"\"\"\n        digits = []\n        while x > 0:\n            remainder = x % base\n            digits.append(str(remainder))\n            x //= base\n        return \"\".join(reversed(digits))\n\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/validator.py\n```\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, InvalidBaseError\n\nclass ValidationService:\n    \"\"\"Centralizes input validation rules for base conversion.\"\"\"\n\n    MIN_BASE: int = 2\n    MAX_BASE: int = 9\n\n    def validate(self, x: int, base: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that x is a non-negative integer and base is within the allowed range.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(x, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input number must be an integer.\")\n        if x < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input number must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n        if not isinstance(base, int):\n            raise InvalidBaseError(\"Base must be an integer.\")\n        if not (self.MIN_BASE <= base <= self.MAX_BASE):\n            raise InvalidBaseError(\n                f\"Base must be an integer between {self.MIN_BASE} and {self.MAX_BASE}, inclusive.\"\n            )\n\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/exceptions.py\n```\nclass InvalidBaseError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid base values.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Invalid base value.\") -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input number values.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Invalid input number.\") -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/dto.py\n```\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass\nclass ConvertRequest:\n    \"\"\"Data transfer object for conversion requests.\"\"\"\n    x: int\n    base: int\n\n@dataclass\nclass ConvertResponse:\n    \"\"\"Data transfer object for conversion responses.\"\"\"\n    result: Optional[str] = None\n    error: Optional[str] = None\n\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/cli.py\n```\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .core import BaseConverter\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, InvalidBaseError\nfrom .utils import parse_int, setup_logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface operations for base conversion.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, converter: Optional[BaseConverter] = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLIController with a BaseConverter instance.\"\"\"\n        self._converter = converter if converter is not None else BaseConverter()\n        setup_logging()\n\n    def run(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses arguments, performs conversion, and prints results or errors.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Convert non-negative integers to a string representation in a specified base (2-9).\"\n        )\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", help=\"Available commands\")\n\n        convert_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n            \"convert\", help=\"Convert a number to a different base.\"\n        )\n        convert_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--x\", type=str, required=True, help=\"The non-negative integer to convert.\"\n        )\n        convert_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--base\", type=str, required=True, help=\"The target base (2-9).\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        if args.command == \"convert\":\n            try:\n                x = parse_int(args.x)\n                base = parse_int(args.base)\n                result = self._converter.convert(x, base)\n                self._print_output(result)\n                return 0\n            except InvalidInputError as e:\n                self._print_error(f\"Error: {e.message}\")\n                logger.error(\"InvalidInputError in CLI: %s\", e.message)\n                return 2  # Specific exit code for invalid input\n            except InvalidBaseError as e:\n                self._print_error(f\"Error: {e.message}\")\n                logger.error(\"InvalidBaseError in CLI: %s\", e.message)\n                return 3  # Specific exit code for invalid base\n            except Exception as e:\n                self._print_error(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n                logger.exception(\"Unexpected error in CLI.\")\n                return 1  # General error\n        else:\n            parser.print_help()\n            return 1\n\n    def _print_output(self, result: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Prints the successful conversion result to stdout.\"\"\"\n        print(result)\n\n    def _print_error(self, msg: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Prints an error message to stderr.\"\"\"\n        print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\n\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/http_adapter.py\n```\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify\n\nfrom .core import BaseConverter\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, InvalidBaseError\nfrom .dto import ConvertRequest, ConvertResponse\nfrom .utils import setup_logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass HTTPController:\n    \"\"\"Flask adapter for exposing the base conversion API over HTTP.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, converter: Optional[BaseConverter] = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the HTTPController with a BaseConverter instance.\"\"\"\n        self._converter = converter if converter is not None else BaseConverter()\n        setup_logging()\n\n    def create_app(self) -> Flask:\n        \"\"\"Creates and configures a Flask application with the /convert endpoint.\"\"\"\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n\n        @app.route('/convert', methods=['POST'])\n        def convert_route():\n            \"\"\"Handles POST requests to /convert for number base conversion.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                payload = request.get_json()\n                if not payload:\n                    raise InvalidInputError(\"Request body must be valid JSON.\")\n\n                x = payload.get(\"x\")\n                base = payload.get(\"base\")\n\n                if x is None or base is None:\n                    raise InvalidInputError(\"Missing 'x' or 'base' in request payload.\")\n\n                # DTO for structured input (can be used for validation too if more complex)\n                request_dto = ConvertRequest(x=x, base=base)\n\n                result_str = self._converter.convert(request_dto.x, request_dto.base)\n                response_dto = ConvertResponse(result=result_str)\n                return jsonify(response_dto.__dict__), 200\n            except (InvalidInputError, InvalidBaseError) as e:\n                logger.warning(\"HTTP API validation error: %s\", e.message)\n                response_dto = ConvertResponse(error=e.message)\n                return jsonify(response_dto.__dict__), 400\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.exception(\"HTTP API unexpected error.\")\n                response_dto = ConvertResponse(error=\"An unexpected internal server error occurred.\")\n                return jsonify(response_dto.__dict__), 500\n        \n        return app\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Entry point for running the HTTP server\n    controller = HTTPController()\n    app = controller.create_app()\n    app.run(debug=False) # In production, use a WSGI server like Gunicorn\n\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/utils.py\n```\nimport logging\nimport sys\n\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef parse_int(value: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Safely parses a string into an integer, raising InvalidInputError on failure.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return int(value)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Cannot parse '{value}' as an integer.\")\n\ndef setup_logging() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Configures basic logging to stdout/stderr.\"\"\"\n    logging.basicConfig(\n        level=logging.INFO,\n        format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s',\n        handlers=[\n            logging.StreamHandler(sys.stdout)\n        ]\n    )\n    # Log errors to stderr\n    error_handler = logging.StreamHandler(sys.stderr)\n    error_handler.setLevel(logging.ERROR)\n    error_handler.setFormatter(logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s'))\n    logging.getLogger().addHandler(error_handler)\n```\n\n```python\nsrc/baseconv/__main__.py\n```\nimport sys\nfrom .cli import CLIController\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    controller = CLIController()\n    sys.exit(controller.run(sys.argv[1:]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```"}
