ramming is fun.\"\n# Output: Prgrmmng s fn.\n```\n\nPipe from stdin:\n\n```bash\necho \"Python is great\" | remove-vowels\n# Output: Pythn s grt\n```\n\nView history:\n\n```bash\nremove-vowels --history --history-count 5\n```\n\n### As an HTTP API\n\nStart the API server (uvicorn is a dependency):\n\n```bash\nuvicorn remove_vowels_app.api:create_api --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThen send requests (e.g., using `curl`):\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8000/remove-vowels \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"text\": \"Hello API!\"}'\n\n# Expected output: {\"result\":\"Hll P!\"}\n```\n\nIf an API key is configured (e.g., in `config.py` or via environment variables), you'd include the `X-API-Key` header:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8000/remove-vowels \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -H \"X-API-Key: your_secret_api_key\" \\\n     -d '{\"text\": \"Secured text.\"}'\n```\n\nAccess API documentation at `http://localhost:8000/docs`.\n\n### Configuration\n\nThe application can be configured by passing an `AppConfig` object to `ApplicationFactory.create()`.\nAlternatively, you can set environment variables (e.g., for `uvicorn` processes):\n- `RV_HISTORY_CAPACITY`: Max number of history entries (default: 100).\n- `RV_JSON_STORE_PATH`: Path to a JSON file for history persistence (e.g., `/var/data/history.json`).\n- `RV_API_KEY`: Secret key for API authentication (e.g., `my_secret_key_123`).\n- `RV_MAX_TEXT_LENGTH`: Max length of input text (default: 10000).\n\nNote: Environment variable parsing for `AppConfig` is not automatically implemented in the generated `config.py` but can be added using libraries like `pydantic-settings`. The `ApplicationFactory` currently uses `DEFAULT_CONFIG` or an explicitly provided `AppConfig` instance.\n\n## Development\n\nTo run tests:\n\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\nTo run linting (e.g., using `ruff` or `flake8`):\n\n```bash\nruff check src tests\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n