{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```python\ndef fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number.\n    >>> fib(10)\n    55\n    >>> fib(1)\n    1\n    >>> fib(8)\n    21\n    \"\"\"\n    # This nested function implements the fast doubling algorithm.\n    # It returns a tuple (F(k), F(k+1)) for the given k.\n    def _fast_doubling_recursive(k: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        if k == 0:\n            return 0, 1  # Base case: F(0) and F(1)\n\n        # Recursively compute F(k/2) and F(k/2 + 1)\n        a, b = _fast_doubling_recursive(k >> 1) \n\n        # Compute F(2k) and F(2k+1) using values from F(k) and F(k+1)\n        c = a * (2 * b - a)  # F(2k)\n        d = a * a + b * b    # F(2k+1)\n\n        if k & 1:  # If k is odd\n            return d, c + d  # F(k) is F(2*(k//2)+1), F(k+1) is F(2*(k//2)+2)\n        else:      # If k is even\n            return c, d      # F(k) is F(2*(k//2)), F(k+1) is F(2*(k//2)+1)\n\n    # The problem statement and doctests imply n >= 0.\n    # The critical requirements forbid adding validation checks.\n    result, _ = _fast_doubling_recursive(n)\n    return result\n```"}
