{"task_id": "HumanEval/83", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# This file is used by Poetry (and potentially other build systems)\n# to define project metadata and dependencies.\n\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"startend\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Counts n-digit positive integers starting or ending with 1.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"startend\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.8\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.30.1\"}\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.2\"\nrequests = \"^2.32.3\" # For API integration testing\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nstartend-count = \"startend.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n```python\n# requirements.txt\n# Runtime dependencies for the project.\n\nfastapi>=0.111.0,<0.112.0\nuvicorn[standard]>=0.30.1,<0.31.0\n\n```\n```python\n# README.md\n# Overview and usage instructions for the StartEndWithOne project.\n\n# StartEndWithOne\n\nThis project provides a Python library, a command-line interface (CLI), and a lightweight HTTP API to compute the count of n-digit positive integers that start or end with digit 1.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Programmatic API**: A Python function to compute the count.\n- **CLI Tool**: A command-line utility for quick computations.\n- **HTTP API**: A simple `GET` endpoint for integration.\n- **Input Validation**: Robust input validation and clear error messages.\n- **Modular Design**: Structured code for maintainability and testability.\n\n## Installation\n\n1.  **Clone the repository (if applicable):**\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/your-repo/startend.git\n    cd startend\n    ```\n\n2.  **Using Poetry (recommended):**\n    If you have Poetry installed:\n    ```bash\n    poetry install\n    poetry shell\n    ```\n\n3.  **Using pip:**\n    ```bash\n    pip install -r requirements.txt\n    # Or, if packaging is set up locally:\n    # pip install .\n    ```\n\n## Usage\n\n### 1. Python API\n\nYou can import the `StartEndService` and use its `compute_count` method:\n\n```python\nfrom src.startend.services import StartEndService\nfrom src.startend.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nservice = StartEndService()\n\ntry:\n    count_for_n_1 = service.compute_count(1)\n    print(f\"Count for n=1: {count_for_n_1}\") # Output: 1\n\n    count_for_n_2 = service.compute_count(2)\n    print(f\"Count for n=2: {count_for_n_2}\") # Output: 18\n\n    count_for_n_3 = service.compute_count(3)\n    print(f\"Count for n=3: {count_for_n_3}\") # Output: 180\n\n    # Example of invalid input\n    count_for_invalid_n = service.compute_count(\"abc\")\nexcept InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n```\n\n### 2. Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nAfter installation, a `startend-count` command will be available:\n\n```bash\n# Valid input\nstartend-count 1\n# Output: {\"n\": 1, \"count\": 1}\n\nstartend-count 2\n# Output: {\"n\": 2, \"count\": 18}\n\nstartend-count 5\n# Output: {\"n\": 5, \"count\": 18000}\n\n# Invalid input\nstartend-count 0\n# Output: Error: Invalid 'n': must be >= 1\n\nstartend-count hello\n# Output: Error: Invalid 'n': must be an integer >= 1\n```\n\n### 3. HTTP API\n\nThe HTTP API is a FastAPI application.\n\n1.  **Run the Uvicorn server:**\n    ```bash\n    uvicorn src.startend.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n    ```\n    The server will typically run on `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.\n\n2.  **Access the endpoint:**\n    Open your browser or use a tool like `curl`:\n\n    ```bash\n    # Valid input\n    curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/count?n=1\n    # Output: {\"n\":1,\"count\":1}\n\n    curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/count?n=2\n    # Output: {\"n\":2,\"count\":18}\n\n    # Invalid input\n    curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/count?n=0\n    # Output: {\"detail\":\"Invalid 'n': must be >= 1\"}\n\n    curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/count?n=foo\n    # Output: {\"detail\":\"Invalid 'n': must be an integer >= 1\"}\n\n    curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/count\n    # Output: {\"detail\":\"query parameter 'n' is required\"}\n    ```\n\n3.  **API Documentation:**\n    FastAPI automatically generates interactive API documentation. While the server is running, visit:\n    -   Swagger UI: `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`\n    -   ReDoc: `http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc`\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 startend/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py         # Package marker; exposes create_app() and StartEndService\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py           # DTO: CountResult\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py         # StartEndService.compute_count()\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 validators.py       # InputValidator.validate_n()\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py      # CLIController and APIController\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 app.py              # FastAPI app factory create_app()\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py       # InvalidInputError\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py            # MathUtils.compute_for_n()\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 cli.py              # CLI entrypoint\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml              # Build metadata and dev dependencies\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt            # Runtime dependencies\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 README.md                   # Project overview and usage\n```\n\n---\n```python\n# src/startend/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Package marker; exposes create_app() and StartEndService.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .app import create_app\nfrom .services import StartEndService\n\n__all__ = [\"create_app\", \"StartEndService\"]\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/models.py\n\"\"\"DTOs and response schemas.\"\"\"\n\nclass CountResult:\n    \"\"\"Data transfer object for count results.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int, count: int) -> None:\n        self.n = n\n        self.count = count\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Returns the result as a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"n\": self.n, \"count\": self.count}\n\nJSON_KEYS = (\"n\", \"count\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"Domain-specific exceptions.\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, status_code: int = 400) -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        self.status_code = status_code\n        super().__init__(message)\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"String representation of the error.\"\"\"\n        return self.message\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/utils.py\n\"\"\"Pure math helpers and formulas.\"\"\"\n\nclass MathUtils:\n    \"\"\"Utility class for mathematical computations.\"\"\"\n    SPECIAL_CASE_N1 = 1\n    MULTIPLIER = 18\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def compute_for_n(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the count of n-digit positive integers that start or end with 1.\n        Assumes n is a positive integer (n >= 1).\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"n must be >= 1 for computation.\")\n        if n == MathUtils.SPECIAL_CASE_N1:\n            return 1\n        return MathUtils.MULTIPLIER * (10 ** (n - 2))\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/validators.py\n\"\"\"Input validation and normalization.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates and normalizes input values.\"\"\"\n    def validate_n(self, n: Any) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if n is an integer and is greater than or equal to 1.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if validation fails.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            n_int = int(n)\n        except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Invalid 'n': must be an integer >= 1\") from exc\n        if n_int < 1:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Invalid 'n': must be >= 1\")\n        return n_int\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/services.py\n\"\"\"Core domain logic for computing counts.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .validators import InputValidator\nfrom .utils import MathUtils\n\nclass StartEndService:\n    \"\"\"Provides the public API for computing counts.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: InputValidator = None) -> None:\n        self._validator = validator or InputValidator()\n\n    def compute_count(self, n: Any) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the count of n-digit positive integers that start or end with 1.\n        Validates input n and then delegates to MathUtils for calculation.\n        \"\"\"\n        n_int = self._validator.validate_n(n)\n        return MathUtils.compute_for_n(n_int)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/controllers.py\n\"\"\"Adapters for CLI and HTTP API.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\nfrom .models import CountResult, JSON_KEYS\nfrom .services import StartEndService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles CLI invocation and output formatting.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: StartEndService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n\n    def run(self, args: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses CLI arguments, computes the count, and prints the result or an error.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for failure).\n        \"\"\"\n        if not args:\n            print(\"Usage: startend-count <n>\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Bad usage\n\n        n_arg = args[0]\n        try:\n            count = self._service.compute_count(n_arg)\n            result = CountResult(n=int(n_arg), count=count)\n            print(json.dumps(result.to_dict()))\n            return 0 # Success\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Invalid input\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # General error\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles HTTP API request/response logic.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: StartEndService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n\n    def get_count(self, n: Any) -> CountResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the count for a given n from an HTTP request.\n        Delegates validation and computation to the service, returns a CountResult DTO.\n        \"\"\"\n        count = self._service.compute_count(n)\n        return CountResult(n=int(n), count=count)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/app.py\n\"\"\"FastAPI application factory and main app instance.\"\"\"\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom .services import StartEndService\nfrom .controllers import APIController\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef create_app(service: StartEndService = None) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates and configures the FastAPI application.\n    Allows injecting a StartEndService for testing.\n    \"\"\"\n    app = FastAPI(title=\"StartOrEndWithOne\", description=\"API to compute n-digit numbers starting or ending with 1.\")\n\n    svc = service or StartEndService()\n    ctrl = APIController(svc)\n\n    @app.get(\n        \"/count\",\n        response_model_by_alias=False, # Allows custom response model if Pydantic is used\n        summary=\"Get count of n-digit numbers starting or ending with 1\",\n        response_description=\"The count for the given n\"\n    )\n    def count_endpoint(n: str):\n        \"\"\"\n        Endpoint to compute the count of n-digit positive integers that start or end with digit 1.\n        - **n**: The number of digits (positive integer, e.g., 1, 2, 3...).\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = ctrl.get_count(n)\n            return result.to_dict()\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=e.status_code, detail=e.message) from e\n    return app\n\n# Module-level instance of the FastAPI app\napp: FastAPI = create_app()\n\n```\n```python\n# src/startend/cli.py\n\"\"\"Console entrypoint wiring.\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\n\n# Import core components\nfrom .services import StartEndService\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\n\ndef main(argv: List[str] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for the command-line interface.\n    Initializes the service and controller, then runs the CLI logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if argv is None:\n        argv = sys.argv[1:]\n\n    # Initialize the core service and CLI controller\n    service = StartEndService()\n    controller = CLIController(service)\n\n    # Run the CLI logic with arguments (excluding the script name itself)\n    return controller.run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n```"}
