{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts sentences starting with 'I'. Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    Leading punctuation and whitespace are ignored before checking the first token.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    SENTENCE_DELIMITERS = {'.', '?', '!'}\n\n    def _split_sentences_internal(text: str) -> list:\n        # Splits text into sentences based on delimiters, keeping delimiters with their sentence.\n        sentences = []\n        if not text:\n            return sentences\n\n        buf = []\n        for char in text:\n            buf.append(char)\n            if char in SENTENCE_DELIMITERS:\n                sentences.append(''.join(buf))\n                buf = []\n        if buf: # Append any remaining text as a sentence.\n            sentences.append(''.join(buf))\n        return sentences\n\n    def _normalize_sentence_internal(sentence_str: str) -> str:\n        # Strips leading/trailing whitespace and surrounding quotes/parentheses/brackets.\n        normalized = sentence_str.strip()\n        return re.sub(r'^[\\'\"\\(\\[]+|[\\'\"\\)\\]]+$', '', normalized).strip()\n\n    def _get_first_token_internal(sentence_str: str) -> str:\n        # Extracts the first whitespace-separated token from a string.\n        parts = sentence_str.split(maxsplit=1)\n        return parts[0] if parts else ''\n\n    boredom_count = 0\n    raw_sentences = _split_sentences_internal(S)\n\n    for sentence in raw_sentences:\n        if not sentence.strip(): # Ignore sentences that are empty or only whitespace.\n            continue\n\n        normalized_sentence = _normalize_sentence_internal(sentence)\n        first_word = _get_first_token_internal(normalized_sentence)\n\n        if first_word == \"I\":\n            boredom_count += 1\n\n    return boredom_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/92", "solution": "```python\ndef any_int(x, y, z):\n    '''\n    Returns true if one of the numbers is equal to the sum of the other two and all numbers are integers, otherwise false.\n    '''\n    if not (x == int(x) and y == int(y) and z == int(z)):\n        return False\n\n    x_int, y_int, z_int = int(x), int(y), int(z)\n    return (x_int == y_int + z_int) or \\\n           (y_int == x_int + z_int) or \\\n           (z_int == x_int + y_int)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/92", "solution": "```python\n# src/any_int_app/__init__.py\nfrom .controllers import any_int\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/any_int_app/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass NumbersInput:\n    \"\"\"Immutable container for three validated integer inputs.\"\"\"\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    z: int\n\n    def to_tuple(self) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the numbers as a tuple.\"\"\"\n        return (self.x, self.y, self.z)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/any_int_app/exceptions.py\nclass AnyIntError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for domain-specific errors in the AnyInt application.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n```\n\n```python\n# src/any_int_app/utils.py\nfrom typing import Any\n\ndef is_integer_like(value: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is an integer or a float with no fractional part, explicitly rejecting booleans.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, bool):\n        return False\n    if isinstance(value, int):\n        return True\n    if isinstance(value, float):\n        return value.is_integer()\n    return False\n```\n\n```python\n# src/any_int_app/validators.py\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\nfrom .models import NumbersInput\nfrom .utils import is_integer_like\nfrom .exceptions import AnyIntError\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates raw inputs for integer-likeness and converts them to NumbersInput.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, strict: bool = False) -> None:\n        self._strict = strict\n\n    def _to_int_if_integer_like(self, value: Any) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts an integer-like value to an int, raises ValueError otherwise.\"\"\"\n        if not is_integer_like(value):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Value '{value}' is not an integer or integer-like float.\")\n        return int(value)\n\n    def validate(self, x: Any, y: Any, z: Any) -> Optional[NumbersInput]:\n        \"\"\"Validates three inputs and returns a NumbersInput object or None.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            xi = self._to_int_if_integer_like(x)\n            yi = self._to_int_if_integer_like(y)\n            zi = self._to_int_if_integer_like(z)\n            return NumbersInput(x=xi, y=yi, z=zi)\n        except ValueError as e:\n            if self._strict:\n                raise AnyIntError(str(e)) from e\n            return None\n```\n\n```python\n# src/any_int_app/services.py\nfrom .models import NumbersInput\n\nclass AnyIntService:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the core business logic to check the sum relation.\"\"\"\n    def is_sum_of_others(self, nums: NumbersInput) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if one of the numbers equals the sum of the other two.\"\"\"\n        return (\n            nums.x == nums.y + nums.z\n            or nums.y == nums.x + nums.z\n            or nums.z == nums.x + nums.y\n        )\n```\n\n```python\n# src/any_int_app/controllers.py\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Any, List, Optional\n\nfrom .validators import InputValidator\nfrom .services import AnyIntService\nfrom .exceptions import AnyIntError\n\nclass AnyIntController:\n    \"\"\"Public API facade orchestrating input validation and business logic.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: Optional[InputValidator] = None, service: Optional[AnyIntService] = None):\n        self._validator = validator or InputValidator(strict=False)\n        self._service = service or AnyIntService()\n\n    def any_int(self, x: Any, y: Any, z: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if one of the three inputs is the sum of the other two, after validation.\"\"\"\n        nums = self._validator.validate(x, y, z)\n        if nums is None:\n            return False\n        return self._service.is_sum_of_others(nums)\n\n    def cli_main(self, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Command-line interface entry point. Parses args, calls any_int, and returns exit code.\"\"\"\n        args = argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:]\n\n        if len(args) != 3:\n            print(\"Usage: any-int-app <number1> <number2> <number3>\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2  # Argument error exit code\n\n        try:\n            # Note: The design specifies `any_int` (the module-level function) for CLI,\n            # but CLI logic is inside the controller. This controller instance will use its\n            # own validator/service, fulfilling the requirement.\n            result = self.any_int(args[0], args[1], args[2])\n            print(result)\n            return 0 if result else 1\n        except AnyIntError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2  # Validation error in strict mode\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n\n# Module-level convenience function\n_controller = AnyIntController()\n\ndef any_int(x: Any, y: Any, z: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Convenience function for the public API.\"\"\"\n    return _controller.any_int(x, y, z)\n\ndef cli_main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"CLI entrypoint, delegates to the controller's cli_main.\"\"\"\n    return _controller.cli_main(argv)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/any_int_app/__main__.py\nimport sys\nfrom .controllers import cli_main\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(cli_main())\n```\n\n```python\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"any-int-app\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small Python library to determine if one of three numbers equals the sum of the other two, with integer validation.\"\nauthors = [\n    { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }\n]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nkeywords = [\"mathematics\", \"integers\", \"utility\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries :: Python Modules\",\n]\n\n[project.scripts]\nany-int-app = \"any_int_app.controllers:cli_main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n```\n\n```python\n# README.md\n# Any Int App\n\nA small, well-tested Python library that determines whether one of three numbers equals the sum of the other two, and all three are integers.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install any-int-app\n```\n(Note: This requires the package to be published to PyPI or installed from a local source.)\n\n## Usage\n\n### Programmatic API\n\nThe main function `any_int` checks the condition with appropriate validation.\n\n```python\nfrom any_int_app import any_int\n\n# Examples from the specification\nprint(f\"any_int(5, 2, 7) \u279e {any_int(5, 2, 7)}\")        # True\nprint(f\"any_int(3, 2, 2) \u279e {any_int(3, 2, 2)}\")        # False\nprint(f\"any_int(3, -2, 1) \u279e {any_int(3, -2, 1)}\")      # True\nprint(f\"any_int(3.6, -2.2, 2) \u279e {any_int(3.6, -2.2, 2)}\") # False\n\n# Edge cases\nprint(f\"any_int(3.0, 2.0, 5.0) \u279e {any_int(3.0, 2.0, 5.0)}\") # True (integer-like floats accepted)\nprint(f\"any_int('a', 2, 3) \u279e {any_int('a', 2, 3)}\")     # False (non-numeric rejected)\nprint(f\"any_int(None, 2, 3) \u279e {any_int(None, 2, 3)}\")    # False (non-numeric rejected)\nprint(f\"any_int(True, 1, 2) \u279e {any_int(True, 1, 2)}\")    # False (booleans explicitly rejected)\n```\n\n### Command Line Interface (CLI)\n\nThe package provides a simple CLI tool `any-int-app` for quick checks.\nIt prints `True` or `False` and exits with code 0 for `True`, 1 for `False`, and 2 for errors.\n\n```bash\nany-int-app 5 2 7\n# Output: True\n# Exit code: 0\n\nany-int-app 3 2 2\n# Output: False\n# Exit code: 1\n\nany-int-app 3.0 2.0 5.0\n# Output: 