{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Returns the closest integer to a numeric string value.\n    Ties are rounded away from zero.\n    '''\n    num = float(value)\n\n    floor_v = math.floor(num)\n    ceil_v = math.ceil(num)\n\n    d_floor = abs(num - floor_v)\n    d_ceil = abs(ceil_v - num)\n\n    if d_floor < d_ceil:\n        return int(floor_v)\n    elif d_ceil < d_floor:\n        return int(ceil_v)\n    else:\n        # Tie-breaking: equidistant, choose the one away from zero (larger absolute value)\n        return int(floor_v if abs(floor_v) > abs(ceil_v) else ceil_v)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a numeric string to the closest integer, rounding ties away from zero.\n    Assumes valid string input representing a finite float.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define a small epsilon for floating-point comparisons, as per design.\n    # This tolerance handles potential inaccuracies when comparing fractional parts to 0.5.\n    DEFAULT_EPS = 1e-12\n\n    # Parse the string value to a float, stripping whitespace.\n    # Critical requirements forbid error handling for invalid input, NaN, or infinity.\n    float_val = float(value.strip())\n\n    # Get the integer part of the float, truncating towards zero (e.g., -14.5 -> -14).\n    base_int_part = math.trunc(float_val)\n\n    # Calculate the absolute fractional part (e.g., 14.5 -> 0.5, -14.5 -> 0.5).\n    fractional_part = abs(float_val - base_int_part)\n\n    # Determine the sign for applying rounding away from zero (e.g., for ties).\n    # math.copysign is used for clarity and correctly handles 0.0, -0.0.\n    sign_val = math.copysign(1, float_val)\n\n    # Apply rounding rules based on the fractional part.\n    # If fractional part is clearly less than 0.5 (outside epsilon range), round towards zero.\n    if fractional_part < 0.5 - DEFAULT_EPS:\n        return int(base_int_part)\n    # If fractional part is clearly greater than 0.5 (outside epsilon range), round away from zero.\n    elif fractional_part > 0.5 + DEFAULT_EPS:\n        return int(base_int_part + sign_val)\n    # Otherwise, the fractional part is effectively 0.5 (within epsilon tolerance), which is a tie.\n    # In tie cases, round away from zero.\n    else:\n        return int(base_int_part + sign_val)\n\n```"}
