{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "def do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates an arithmetic expression built from lists of operators and integer operands.\n    Supports +, -, *, //, ** with correct precedence and associativity.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    op_precedence = {\n        '+': 2, '-': 2,\n        '*': 3, '//': 3,\n        '**': 4\n    }\n\n    op_associativity = {\n        '+': 'left', '-': 'left',\n        '*': 'left', '//': 'left',\n        '**': 'right'\n    }\n\n    def _apply_operator(op, left, right):\n        if op == '+':\n            return left + right\n        elif op == '-':\n            return left - right\n        elif op == '*':\n            return left * right\n        elif op == '//':\n            return left // right\n        elif op == '**':\n            return left ** right\n        return 0 # Should not be reached with valid inputs\n\n    # Combine operands and operators into a single token list\n    tokens = []\n    operand_idx = 0\n    operator_idx = 0\n    while operand_idx < len(operand):\n        tokens.append(operand[operand_idx])\n        operand_idx += 1\n        if operator_idx < len(operator):\n            tokens.append(operator[operator_idx])\n            operator_idx += 1\n\n    # Shunting-yard algorithm to convert to Reverse Polish Notation (RPN)\n    output_queue = []\n    operator_stack = []\n\n    for token in tokens:\n        if isinstance(token, int):\n            output_queue.append(token)\n        else: # token is an operator string\n            while (operator_stack and operator_stack[-1] in op_precedence and\n                   (op_precedence[operator_stack[-1]] > op_precedence[token] or\n                    (op_precedence[operator_stack[-1]] == op_precedence[token] and op_associativity[token] == 'left'))):\n                output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n            operator_stack.append(token)\n\n    while operator_stack:\n        output_queue.append(operator_stack.pop())\n\n    # Evaluate the RPN expression\n    evaluation_stack = []\n    for token in output_queue:\n        if isinstance(token, int):\n            evaluation_stack.append(token)\n        else: # token is an operator string\n            right_operand = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            left_operand = evaluation_stack.pop()\n            result = _apply_operator(token, left_operand, right_operand)\n            evaluation_stack.append(result)\n\n    return evaluation_stack[0]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "```python\ndef do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates an algebraic expression from lists of operators and operands,\n    respecting standard operator precedence and left-to-right associativity.\n    Assumes valid inputs as per the problem constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_operands = list(operand)\n    current_operators = list(operator)\n\n    # Define operator precedence levels and groups for processing\n    # Higher number means higher precedence.\n    precedence = {'**': 3, '*': 2, '//': 2, '+': 1, '-': 1}\n    \n    # Process operations by precedence, from highest to lowest\n    # This loop ensures correct evaluation order for **, then *, //, then +, -\n    for op_precedence_level in sorted(set(precedence.values()), reverse=True):\n        i = 0\n        while i < len(current_operators):\n            op = current_operators[i]\n            if precedence[op] == op_precedence_level:\n                # Perform the operation\n                left_val = current_operands[i]\n                right_val = current_operands[i+1]\n                \n                if op == '+':\n                    result = left_val + right_val\n                elif op == '-':\n                    result = left_val - right_val\n                elif op == '*':\n                    result = left_val * right_val\n                elif op == '//':\n                    result = left_val // right_val\n                elif op == '**':\n                    result = left_val ** right_val\n                \n                # Update the operand list with the result and remove the consumed operand\n                current_operands[i] = result\n                current_operands.pop(i + 1)\n                # Remove the operator that was just applied\n                current_operators.pop(i)\n                # Do not increment i; re-evaluate at the current index as lists have shifted\n                # This inherently handles left-to-right associativity for same-precedence operators\n            else:\n                i += 1 # Move to the next operator\n    \n    return current_operands[0]\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "```python\ndef solve(s):\n    \"\"\"You are given a string s.\n    if s[i] is a letter, reverse its case from lower to upper or vise versa, \n    otherwise keep it as it is.\n    If the string contains no letters, reverse the string.\n    The function should return the resulted string.\n    Examples\n    solve(\"1234\") = \"4321\"\n    solve(\"ab\") = \"AB\"\n    solve(\"#a@C\") = \"#A@c\"\n    \"\"\"\n    contains_alpha = False\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            contains_alpha = True\n            break\n\n    if not contains_alpha:\n        return s[::-1]\n    else:\n        transformed_chars = []\n        for char in s:\n            if char.isalpha():\n                transformed_chars.append(char.swapcase())\n            else:\n                transformed_chars.append(char)\n        return \"\".join(transformed_chars)\n```"}
