{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "```python\ndef generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_digits = {0, 2, 4, 6, 8}\n    start = min(a, b)\n    end = max(a, b)\n    \n    result = sorted(d for d in even_digits if start <= d <= end)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/5", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef intersperse(numbers: List[int], delimeter: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Insert a number 'delimeter' between every two consecutive elements of input list `numbers`.\n    Handles empty and single-element lists as specified.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    it = iter(numbers)\n    result.append(next(it))  # Add the first element\n\n    for x in it:\n        result.append(delimeter)  # Add the delimiter\n        result.append(x)         # Add the next element\n\n    return result"}
